    "model": "John Devoy was born in Co. Kildare in 1842 and joined the Irish Republican Brotherhood in the 1860s. He was sentenced to 15 years for treason-felony in 1866 and released in 1871 on condition that he went into exile. In 1878 he proposed the New Departure with Michael Davitt, a plan for Fenians to work with Parnell's constitutional nationalists. He founded the Gaelic American in New York in 1903 and edited it to keep Irish-American opinion behind the republican cause.",
    "model_source": "haiku",
    "answerStatus": "written",
    "type": [
     "long-answer"
    ],
    "diagramRelation": "none",
    "offSpec": false,
