    "label": "B3",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Ireland applied for UN membership in 1946, but a Soviet veto blocked it until Ireland was admitted on 14 December 1955. Frank Aiken's Irish resolutions from 1958 led to Resolution 1665 in 1961, which called on states not to acquire nuclear weapons. Ireland was the first state to sign the 1968 Non-Proliferation Treaty. Irish troops joined the UN force in the Congo in 1960, and about 6,000 served there until 1964, when twenty-six had died.",
    "model_source": "haiku",
    "answerStatus": "written",
