    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Piedmont-Sardinia under Cavour became the leader of the movement for unity after he became prime minister in 1852 and modernised its economy and army. Cavour secured French help at Plombières in 1858, and France fought with Piedmont against Austria in 1859, which gave Lombardy to Piedmont. In 1860 Tuscany, Modena, Parma and the Romagna voted to join Piedmont, and Garibaldi's Thousand conquered Sicily and Naples. The Kingdom of Italy was proclaimed on 17 March 1861 under Victor Emmanuel II, with Venetia and Rome added later.",
