    "label": "C4",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Mikhail Gorbachev became General Secretary of the Communist Party on 11 March 1985 and launched glasnost, greater openness, and perestroika, a restructuring of the economy. He chose not to use force to keep eastern European states under Soviet control, so communist rule ended in 1989 in largely peaceful transfers. He withdrew Soviet troops from Afghanistan by February 1989, ending a costly war. With Reagan he signed the INF Treaty on 8 December 1987, which eliminated US and Soviet intermediate-range missiles. He introduced partly free elections in March 1989, and in 1990 the party gave up its constitutional monopoly of power. His reforms weakened central control, and the Soviet Union was dissolved on 26 December 1991, a day after he resigned as president.",
