    "label": "C3",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Monroe became a major star in 1953 with Gentlemen Prefer Blondes, and The Seven Year Itch (1955) made her one of the most popular box office stars of the decade. Her glamorous image was widely copied in advertising and tied her to the consumer culture of the 1950s. In 1955 she founded Marilyn Monroe Productions, and she won acclaim for her comic role in Some Like It Hot (1959). Later feminist critics read her image as a product of a male-dominated film industry that limited women to decorative roles. She sang Happy Birthday, Mr President to John F. Kennedy in May 1962, and she died in August 1962 from an overdose of barbiturates. Historians now treat her as a symbol of both the glamour and the constraints placed on women in the 1950s.",
