    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Molly Maguires were a secret society of Irish miners in the anthracite coalfields of eastern Pennsylvania, especially Schuylkill County, in the 1860s and 1870s. Violence against mine bosses and police was blamed on them, and they were accused of murders and arson. The owner of the Reading Railroad, Franklin B. Gowen, hired the Pinkerton detective James McParland, who infiltrated the society. Twenty men were hanged between 1877 and 1879, and ten of them were hanged on 21 June 1877, known as the Day of the Rope.",
