    "model": "Daniel Mannix was born in Charleville, Co. Cork, in 1864 and trained at Maynooth, where he was president from 1903 to 1912. He was appointed coadjutor archbishop of Melbourne in 1912 and became archbishop in 1917. During the First World War he opposed conscription and led the campaign in the referendums of 1916 and 1917, which were both defeated. He supported Irish independence and criticised British policy in Ireland after 1916, which made him a target for loyalist opinion in Australia.",
