    "model": "Maureen O'Hara was born in Ranelagh, Dublin, in 1920, and trained at the Abbey Theatre school before moving to Britain and then America. She appeared in How Green Was My Valley in 1941 and in Miracle on 34th Street in 1947, which established her as a major star. She worked repeatedly with John Ford, and their films included Rio Grande in 1950. Historians note that her screen image of the spirited Irish woman was partly a Hollywood creation.",
