    "label": "B2",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Lynch became Taoiseach on 10 November 1966 as a compromise choice, and he won the 1969 general election with a majority of seats. After the violence of August 1969 he said the state could not stand by, but he ruled out sending troops across the border. In May 1970 he dismissed Charles Haughey and Neil Blaney over the Arms Crisis, which tested his authority. His 1977 government cut taxes and increased borrowed spending, which led to a crisis by 1979 and to his resignation.",
    "model_source": "haiku",
