    "label": "B2",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Mazzini, born in Genoa in 1805, joined the Carbonari before his arrest and exile in 1830. In 1831 he founded Young Italy at Marseille, a secret society that aimed at a unified Italian republic. He wanted a republic with the people as sovereign, under the motto God and the People, and his book The Duties of Man stressed duty to the nation. He returned in 1848 and was one of the triumvirs who governed the Roman Republic of 1849, but his unified republic was never achieved.",
