    "label": "B2",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Soviet Union blockaded road, rail and canal access to West Berlin from June 1948 to cut the Western sectors off from supplies. The Western powers organised an airlift that flew food, fuel and other supplies into the city through the Tempelhof, Gatow and Tegel airfields. Planes sometimes landed about every minute, and the airlift delivered over two million tons of supplies. The Soviet Union lifted the blockade on 12 May 1949, and the crisis ended without war.",
