    "model": "English spread across the world through the British Empire and the Commonwealth and became the official language of many former British colonies, including Nigeria and Kenya. After 1945 American economic and cultural power, through films, music, business and international organisations, further spread the use of English. In Nigeria English is the language of government, education and the courts, and it is a second language for many people alongside local languages. In India Hindi was declared the official language in 1950, but English remained an associate official language and was kept after anti-Hindi protests in Tamil Nadu in 1965.",
