    "label": "B4",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Achmad Sukarno was born on 6 June 1901 in East Java, trained as an engineer and founded the Indonesian Nationalist Party in 1927. The Dutch imprisoned him in 1929 and later exiled him, and under the Japanese occupation he worked with the Japanese administration and encouraged mass mobilisation. He proclaimed Indonesian independence with Hatta in Jakarta on 17 August 1945 and became the first president of the Republic. From 1959 his Guided Democracy replaced parliamentary government with presidential rule, and by 1965 his economy and his policy of confrontation with Malaysia had left Indonesia isolated.",
