    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Ben-Gurion emigrated to Ottoman Palestine in 1906 and worked as a labour activist among the Jewish community there. He led the executive of the Jewish Agency from 1935 and built support for a Jewish state. He accepted the 1947 UN partition plan as a first step towards a Jewish state. On 14 May 1948 he proclaimed the State of Israel in Tel Aviv and became its first prime minister. He oversaw the creation of the Israel Defence Forces, ordering the shelling of the Irgun ship Altalena in June 1948 to establish one army. In October 1956 he attended the secret talks at Sevres with Britain and France, which planned the invasion of Egypt.",
