    "model": "Fidel Castro took power in Cuba on 1 January 1959 and in 1960 nationalised US-owned sugar, oil and other property. Eisenhower cut the Cuban sugar quota in July 1960, imposed a trade embargo and broke off diplomatic relations in January 1961, so Cuba turned to the Soviet Union for trade and oil. CIA-trained Cuban exiles landed at the Bay of Pigs on 17 April 1961 and were defeated within three days. During the missile crisis of October 1962 Kennedy imposed a naval quarantine, and Khrushchev agreed to remove the Soviet missiles in return for a US pledge not to invade Cuba.",
