    "label": "C1",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Truman became president on 12 April 1945 when Roosevelt died, and he faced a wave of strikes as the wartime economy was converted to peacetime production. His Fair Deal of 1949 proposed national health insurance and a wider Social Security system, but Congress blocked most of it. The Truman Doctrine of March 1947 and the Marshall Plan of 1948 committed the United States to containing Soviet expansion and rebuilding Western Europe. He helped to found NATO in April 1949, and in June 1950 he sent American forces to defend South Korea without a vote in Congress. Executive Order 9981 of July 1948 ordered the desegregation of the armed forces, which began his civil rights programme. He recognised the new state of Israel on 14 May 1948, and he won a surprise victory over Thomas Dewey in 1948.",
