    "label": "C4",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Edward Galvin, a Cork priest, went to China in 1912 as a missionary priest. In 1916 he founded the Maynooth Mission to China with Father John Blowick, and the first Irish missionaries went to China in 1920. He led the mission in the Hanyang area of Hubei province and became a bishop in 1927 as vicar apostolic of Hanyang. The mission ran churches, schools, orphanages and clinics, and it trained Chinese catechists and priests. He led the mission through civil conflict and the Japanese invasion, in which Hanyang was bombed. After the Communist takeover in 1949 he was placed under house arrest, expelled in 1952, and he died at Dalgan Park in 1956.",
