    "label": "C4",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Breandán Ó hEithir was born on Inis Mór in 1930 and became a journalist and broadcaster with RTÉ, presenting current affairs and sport in Irish and English. His satirical novel Lig Sinn i gCathú, about a Galway student, was widely read in Irish, and he translated it himself as Lead Us into Temptation in 1978. Over the Bar (1984) was a personal history of the GAA, and The Begrudger's Guide to Irish Politics (1986) was a witty account of political life. He wrote about Irish as a living medium for modern subjects, not as a duty, and he bridged the Gaeltacht and the English-speaking world. Contemporaries valued him as a rare Irish-language writer with a wide readership. Later critics see him as one of the most accomplished bilingual writers and broadcasters of his generation.",
