    "label": "B3",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Louis-Napoleon, nephew of Napoleon I, was elected president of the Second Republic in December 1848 with about three-quarters of the vote. He seized power in a coup on 2 December 1851, dissolved the Assembly and was approved by a plebiscite, and in 1852 he became Emperor Napoleon III. His regime brought rapid economic growth and rebuilt Paris, and the Cobden-Chevalier Treaty with Britain in 1860 reduced tariffs. His foreign policy failed, as the Mexican empire collapsed by 1867, and he was captured at Sedan in 1870, after which the Second Empire fell.",
