    "label": "B4",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Darwin was born in Shrewsbury in 1809, studied medicine and then divinity, and joined HMS Beagle as naturalist in 1831. On the Beagle he collected fossils, plants and animals and observed how species varied in South America, the Galápagos and Australia. He published On the Origin of Species in November 1859, arguing that species change through natural selection and that all living things share common ancestors. The Descent of Man in 1871 applied evolution to human origins, and his work made him the founder of modern evolutionary biology.",
