    "model": "Bakunin, born in 1814 into a Russian noble family, left the army and became a revolutionary in the 1840s. He joined the Slav Congress in Prague in 1848 and then the Dresden rising of May 1849, after which he was sentenced to death, later commuted to life imprisonment. He was handed over to Austria and then Russia in 1851 and held in the Peter and Paul Fortress, then exiled to Siberia in 1857. He escaped in 1861 by way of Japan and the United States to London. He argued for the abolition of the state and all authority, a position that became known as anarchism. His rivalry with Marx split the First International, which expelled him at the Hague Congress in 1872.",
