    "label": "C4",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Bismarck became Minister-President of Prussia in September 1862 and governed for years without an approved budget during the army reform conflict. He used the Danish War of 1864 with Austria to take Schleswig and Holstein, and the Gastein settlement of 1865 set up a conflict with Austria. He secured Italian support through an alliance in April 1866, and after Königgrätz he persuaded William I not to take Austrian territory. The Treaty of Prague in August 1866 dissolved the German Confederation and excluded Austria, and the North German Confederation under Prussian leadership was formed in 1867. He used the edited Ems telegram in July 1870 to provoke France into war, which brought the southern German states in on the Prussian side. The German Empire was proclaimed at Versailles on 18 January 1871, with William I as emperor.",
