    "model": "Serbia became fully independent in 1878, and its drive to unite the South Slavs threatened Austria-Hungary, which had millions of South Slavs in its empire. After the murder of King Alexander Obrenović in 1903 the new Serbian government turned towards Russia and France rather than Vienna. Austria-Hungary's Pig War of 1906 closed its market to Serbian livestock, but Serbia found new markets in Germany, Italy and France. Austria-Hungary annexed Bosnia in 1908, and Serbia had to back down in 1909 after Germany warned Russia to accept the annexation. The Balkan Wars of 1912 to 1913 doubled Serbia's size, and Austria-Hungary was alarmed by a stronger Serbia that wanted an Adriatic port.",
