    "label": "B4",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Vichy regime banned strikes, dissolved the trade unions and introduced a Labour Charter in 1941, while the Legion of French Combatants replaced a mass party. Vichy passed its first anti-Jewish statute in October 1940 without German demand, excluding Jews from public office and many professions. The Milice, a paramilitary force founded in January 1943, hunted members of the Resistance and carried out reprisals against civilians. The British attack on the French fleet at Mers-el-Kébir on 3 July 1940 turned many Vichy supporters against Britain, and the Germans occupied the whole south in November 1942.",
