    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Michael Davitt was born at Straide, Co. Mayo, in 1846, and his family was evicted when he was a child. He joined the IRB and was sentenced to fifteen years for arms trafficking, but he was released in December 1877. In 1878 he met John Devoy in the USA, and their New Departure linked Fenians, land reformers and Home Rule supporters. He organised the Irishtown meeting in April 1879 and helped found the Land League of Mayo. He wanted land nationalisation rather than peasant proprietorship, and he rejected violence against individuals.",
