    "model": "Before 1967 most children left school at fourteen, and the Investment in Education report of 1965 showed wide differences in participation by class and region. Donogh O'Malley announced free second-level education in 1966, and it began in September 1967 with free school transport. Comprehensive schools offering academic and practical subjects to all abilities opened from 1966. The Higher Education Authority was set up in 1968, and a grants scheme helped students from poorer homes reach university, so third-level numbers grew strongly in the 1970s.",
