    "model": "Pope John Paul II reaffirmed traditional Catholic teaching on contraception, abortion and the priesthood, which many saw as a conservative turn after the Council. He opposed the ordination of women and any change to clerical celibacy, and the Congregation for the Doctrine of the Faith under Cardinal Ratzinger disciplined theologians from 1981. He travelled more than any previous pope, making over a hundred foreign journeys and drawing huge crowds in Poland, Latin America, Africa and Europe. He visited Ireland in 1979 and appealed to paramilitaries at Drogheda to end the violence in Northern Ireland. He launched World Youth Days in the mid-1980s and promoted new movements such as Opus Dei and the Neocatechumenal Way. He visited the Great Synagogue of Rome in 1986 and called Jews the elder brothers of Catholics.",
