    "model": "In 1958 de Gaulle returned to power after the May crisis in Algiers, and at first the settlers believed he would keep Algeria French. On 16 September 1959 he offered Algerians self-determination, a choice between independence, integration with France and association. The referendum of 8 January 1961 approved self-determination by about 75 per cent of the votes cast overall, and he defeated the Algiers putsch of April 1961 with the loyal army. The Evian Accords of 18 March 1962 ended the war, and Algeria became independent on 5 July 1962.",
