    "label": "B4",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Mobutu was chief of staff of the Congolese army from July 1960 and led the coup of 14 September 1960 that neutralised both Lumumba and Kasa-Vubu. He seized power again on 24 November 1965 and ruled as president under a one-party system through his Popular Movement of the Revolution. In 1971 he renamed the Congo Zaire, and in 1973 Zairianisation transferred foreign-owned plantations and businesses to Zairian owners, mostly his associates. The United States, Belgium and France supported him as a barrier to communism in central Africa, but he announced the end of the one-party state in 1990 under pressure and stayed in power until 1997.",
