    "model": "Development workers faced poor roads and limited supplies, which made it hard to reach rural communities. Cultural misunderstandings with local communities often complicated their work. Many were young volunteers on short contracts, with limited access to medicine, transport and communications. Civil wars brought the risk of violence to workers in the field. Projects were difficult to keep running once the donor had left. Historians later criticised the top-down projects of the 1960s and 1970s, which had been planned without local people.",
