    "model": "Breandán Ó hEithir was a journalist and broadcaster with RTÉ who presented current affairs and sport in Irish and English. His satirical novel Lig Sinn i gCathú was widely read in Irish, and he translated it himself as Lead Us into Temptation in 1978. His books Over the Bar (1984), a history of the GAA, and The Begrudger's Guide to Irish Politics (1986) reached a wide readership. Sylvia Meehan was appointed in 1977 as the first chairperson of the Employment Equality Agency, which she led until 1992. The agency's research into education, pay, maternity leave and childcare helped to shape later legislation, and Meehan supervised investigations into discrimination at work. Both helped change Irish life, Ó hEithir by bringing Irish-language writing to a modern audience and Meehan by putting equality laws into practice.",
