    "model": "Mazzini founded Young Italy at Marseille in 1831 to win a unified republic, but his risings failed and Piedmont's armies were defeated at Custoza and Novara in 1848 and 1849. From 1852 Cavour made Piedmont the leader of the national cause, and at Plombières in 1858 Napoleon III agreed to help Piedmont against Austria in return for Nice and Savoy. In 1860 Tuscany, Modena, Parma and the Romagna voted to join Piedmont, and Garibaldi's Thousand conquered Sicily and Naples. The Kingdom of Italy was proclaimed on 17 March 1861, and Venetia and Rome were added in 1866 and 1870.",
