    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Charles de Gaulle was born in Lille in 1890 and became leader of the Free French with his appeal from London on 18 June 1940. He headed the provisional government from 1944 to January 1946 and founded the Rally of the French People in 1947. He returned to power in 1958, and in 1959 he offered Algerians self-determination, moving towards ending the Algerian war. He kept French influence in sub-Saharan Africa through the French Community and co-operation accords, working with his adviser Jacques Foccart.",
