    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Church membership rose sharply in the 1950s, and Congress added the words under God to the Pledge of Allegiance in June 1954. Religion was seen as a bulwark against communism, and a law of 1956 made In God We Trust the national motto. Televangelists such as Jerry Falwell and Pat Robertson built large audiences through television, using it to raise money and promote political messages. The Moral Majority, founded in 1979, mobilised conservative Christians behind Ronald Reagan's campaign in 1980 on issues such as abortion and school prayer.",
