    "label": "3(a)",
    "marks": 10,
    "model": "In 1967 Document A describes the march as 'a great folk festival' with 'good humour'.\nBy 1969 Document B says Catholics were 'sick of Protestants and police cordons and riot tenders and drumbeating'.\nDocument B also says most Catholics stayed at home but were 'irritated, ill-humoured and apprehensive'.\nThe contrast shows that sectarian tension had risen sharply between the two marches, with the Bogside feeling oppressed rather than amused.",
