    "model": "The Gaelic League was founded in Dublin in July 1893 by Douglas Hyde and Eoin MacNeill, with Hyde as president. It set out to revive the Irish language and presented itself as non-political and non-sectarian. Branches ran Irish classes, and travelling teachers called timirí went to rural areas, with several hundred branches by 1904. From 1897 the League held the annual Oireachtas, and its weekly An Claidheamh Soluis began in 1899. Its campaigns won Irish a place in primary schools by the Revised Programme of 1900 and made Irish compulsory for matriculation to the National University from 1913.",
    "model_source": "haiku",
    "answerStatus": "written",
    "type": [
     "long-answer"
    ],
    "diagramRelation": "none",
