    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Investment in Education, published in 1965, showed that participation in education varied widely by social class and region. Donogh O'Malley announced free second-level education in September 1966, and fees were abolished in participating schools from 1967 along with free school transport. The Health Act 1970 set up eight regional health boards, which began work in 1971 and took over the functions of the old county health authorities. Contributory old age pensions were introduced in 1961, and pay-related benefit for unemployed and sick workers followed in 1974.",
