    "label": "C4",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Garret FitzGerald led Fine Gael from 1977 and was Taoiseach from June 1981 to March 1982 and again from December 1982 to March 1987. In 1981 he launched a constitutional crusade to make the Republic more pluralist, though he had not wished to see the Eighth Amendment written in the form that was passed in 1983. In 1985 his government liberalised the contraception law, allowing sale without prescription to people over 18. He negotiated the Anglo-Irish Agreement with Margaret Thatcher, which he signed at Hillsborough in November 1985 and which gave Dublin a consultative role in Northern Ireland. Sylvia Meehan was the first chairperson of the Employment Equality Agency, appointed in 1977 and serving until 1992. Through the Agency's investigations and research into pay, education and maternity leave she helped turn the equality laws into practice.",
