    "label": "B3",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "On 10 July 1940 the National Assembly gave Marshal Pétain full powers, which ended the Third Republic and created the Vichy state in the unoccupied south of France. The regime called its programme the National Revolution, replaced Liberté, Égalité, Fraternité with Travail, Famille, Patrie, and ended elections and strikes. Vichy collaborated actively with Germany, and it passed anti-Jewish laws in October 1940 without any German demand. About 76,000 Jews were deported from France, and the Milice, founded in January 1943, hunted members of the Resistance.",
