    "label": "C2",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "In October 1933 Hitler left the League of Nations, and in March 1935 he announced conscription and an air force in breach of Versailles. The Anglo-German Naval Agreement of June 1935 allowed a German navy about 35 per cent of Britain's size, and Britain accepted it without consulting France. He reoccupied the Rhineland in March 1936 and annexed Austria in March 1938, and Britain and France offered no military resistance. At Munich in September 1938 Britain and France accepted the German takeover of the Sudetenland, and Czechoslovakia was not consulted. Hitler occupied Prague in March 1939, which ended British appeasement, and the Nazi-Soviet Pact of August 1939 removed the threat of a war on two fronts. He invaded Poland on 1 September 1939, and Britain and France declared war two days later.",
