    "marks": 30,
    "model": "In June 1948 the Soviet Union blockaded road, rail and canal access to West Berlin after the Western powers introduced the Deutsche Mark in their zones. Stalin wanted the Western powers to give up the new currency and their plans for a West German state, or to leave Berlin. The Western powers responded with an airlift that flew food, fuel and other supplies into the city from the airfields at Tempelhof, Gatow and Tegel. Over two million tons were delivered, and the blockade was lifted on 12 May 1949 after Truman had refused to withdraw from Berlin.",
