    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Gandhi returned from South Africa in 1915 and became the dominant leader of the Indian National Congress after 1920. He developed satyagraha, a method of non-violent civil disobedience, and first used it in peasant campaigns at Champaran and Kheda. He led mass campaigns such as the Non-Cooperation movement of 1920 to 1922 and the Salt March of 1930 to the sea at Dandi. His Quit India campaign of 1942 showed Britain that its authority could not be maintained by force alone.",
