    "model": "Truman's loyalty programme of March 1947 and the House Un-American Activities Committee hearings on Hollywood in October 1947 began the red scare, and the Hollywood Ten were jailed for contempt of Congress. McCarthy's Wheeling speech of 9 February 1950 claimed to hold a list of communists in the State Department, and it made him a national figure. The Tydings Committee called his claims a fraud, but his attacks helped to defeat Senator Millard Tydings in the November 1950 election. The Army-McCarthy hearings of 1954 were televised, and the Senate censured him on 2 December 1954 by 67 votes to 22.",
