    "model": "The Nuremberg Rallies were the annual Reichsparteitag of the Nazi party, beginning with a large rally in August 1927, and they aimed to create emotional bonds between the leader, the party and the German people. The city's medieval imperial history let the Nazis link the regime with the German past. The rallies turned party gatherings into national spectacles, with mass parades of the SA, SS and Hitler Youth and Speer's cathedral of light from 1934. The 1935 rally announced the Nuremberg Laws, so the rallies publicised the regime's racial policies to the German public. Riefenstahl's film Triumph of the Will extended the rallies to cinemas in Germany and abroad. Foreign visitors were impressed by the order and vitality of the new Germany, which showed the regime's unity.",
