    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Berlin Crisis began in June 1948 when the Soviet Union cut off road, rail and canal links to the Western sectors of Berlin. It was caused by the Western currency reform of 20 June 1948, which introduced the Deutsche Mark, and by Stalin's wish to drive the Western powers out of the city. The Western allies flew supplies into West Berlin from airfields such as Tempelhof and Tegel, landing planes about every minute at the busiest times. The crisis ended on 12 May 1949 when the Soviets lifted the blockade, and the West had shown that it would not give up Berlin.",
