    "label": "C1",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Truman authorised the atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki in August 1945, shortly after he had met Stalin at Potsdam. The Truman Doctrine of 12 March 1947 pledged US support for free peoples resisting communist pressure, first applied to Greece and Turkey. The Marshall Plan of 1948 to 1952 gave about 13 billion dollars in aid to Western Europe, and the Berlin airlift defeated the Soviet blockade of West Berlin from June 1948 to May 1949. He recognised the new state of Israel on 14 May 1948, within minutes of its declaration of independence. NATO was founded in April 1949, and NSC-68 in April 1950 called for a large build-up of defence strength. He sent US forces to defend South Korea in June 1950 without a congressional vote, and he dismissed MacArthur in April 1951 after the general publicly argued for attacking China.",
