    "label": "2(b)",
    "marks": 10,
    "model": "Yes, there is clear evidence of racism in both documents.\nDocument A shows the Congolese man frantically cutting the rope, unaware that he will fall too, which suggests he has lesser intelligence because he is black.\nBy contrast, the Belgian is shown as foolish and out of his depth.\nDocument B shows the paratroopers refusing a truce rather than share duties with Congolese soldiers, using racist insults.\nA paratrooper apologised to Lee Griggs for shooting at him because he thought he was an African, which suggests Griggs's life was worth more than an African's.",
