    "label": "C4",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Bernadette Devlin helped to form People's Democracy at Queen's University Belfast in October 1968, after the Derry march, and she took part in the Belfast to Derry march that was attacked at Burntollet Bridge on 4 January 1969. She was elected MP for Mid Ulster at a by-election in April 1969, aged twenty-one. On 31 January 1972, the day after Bloody Sunday, she struck the Home Secretary, Reginald Maudling, in the House of Commons. Ian Paisley founded the Free Presbyterian Church in 1951 and led the 'O'Neill must go' campaign from 1966, which pressed for the Prime Minister's removal. He founded the Democratic Unionist Party in 1971, opposed the Sunningdale Agreement and supported the 1974 strike. He also led protests against the Anglo-Irish Agreement of 1985.",
