    "marks": 30,
    "model": "In 1966 the first comprehensive schools opened, including schools at Carraroe and Cootehill, offering academic and practical subjects in areas that lacked second-level schools. Donogh O'Malley's scheme for free second-level education, announced in September 1966, began in 1967 and ended fees in participating schools. The Health Act 1970 set up eight regional health boards, which began work in 1971 and took over the functions of the county health authorities. Contributory old age pensions for insured workers were introduced in 1961, and free travel for pensioners followed in 1967.",
