    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Second Vatican Council, held from 1962 to 1965, allowed the Mass to be said in the vernacular, and the first Masses in English in Ireland were celebrated in 1965. Priests began to face the congregation, and laypeople were allowed to act as readers and distribute communion. The council promoted ecumenism, and the Catholic ban on attending Trinity College Dublin was lifted in 1970. It declared that religious freedom was a right, which weakened the claim that a Catholic state should have a special position in law.",
