    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Garret FitzGerald was born in 1926 and was Minister for Foreign Affairs from 1973 to 1977. He became Fine Gael leader in 1977 and was Taoiseach from 1981 to 1982 and again from 1982 to 1987. In 1981 he announced a constitutional crusade to make the Republic more pluralist, including divorce reform and the removal of Catholic influences from the law. He set up the New Ireland Forum in 1983 and negotiated the Anglo-Irish Agreement with Margaret Thatcher in 1985.",
