    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Giuseppe Mazzini was born in Genoa in 1805 and joined the Carbonari before his arrest and exile in 1830. In 1831 he founded Young Italy at Marseille to work for a unified Italian republic. His motto was God and the People, and he believed Italy must be freed by the people's own insurrection rather than by kings or foreign help. He organised a failed invasion of Savoy in 1834. In 1849 he governed Rome as one of the triumvirs of the Roman Republic.",
