    "label": "C4",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Bismarck became Minister-President of Prussia in 1862 and pushed through army reform without an approved budget. He led Prussia into the Danish War of 1864 alongside Austria, and Denmark gave up the duchies of Schleswig and Holstein. He secured Italian support for war against Austria with an alliance in April 1866. After Prussia's victory at Königgrätz in July 1866, the Treaty of Prague excluded Austria from German affairs. He became Chancellor of the North German Confederation in 1867, under Prussian leadership. He edited the Ems telegram in 1870 to provoke France into war, which drew the southern states into the struggle. The German Empire was proclaimed at Versailles on 18 January 1871, and Bismarck became Imperial Chancellor.",
