    "label": "B2",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "OPEC's Gulf members raised the oil price by about 70 per cent on 16 October 1973, and prices roughly quadrupled in the following months. The Arab oil producers announced an embargo on exports to the USA and then to the Netherlands, as supporters of Israel. Western European governments introduced fuel rationing and car-free Sundays, and Britain brought in a three-day working week from January to March 1974. Unemployment and inflation rose together, producing stagflation, and governments abandoned the post-war commitment to full employment to focus on defeating inflation.",
