    "label": "B2",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Downing Street Declaration was issued on 15 December 1993 by John Major and Albert Reynolds. It stated that the Irish people as a whole had the right to self-determination, and that a united Ireland would require the consent of a majority in Northern Ireland. It said that Britain had no selfish strategic or economic interest in Northern Ireland and would legislate for a united Ireland if a majority wished it. It invited republicans to renounce violence and join talks, and the Irish government agreed to examine Articles 2 and 3 of its constitution.",
