    "label": "B2",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Before 1967 most children left school at 14, because secondary schools charged fees and were mostly owned by religious orders. Investment in Education, published in 1965, showed wide differences in participation by social class and region. Donogh O'Malley announced free second-level education in September 1966, and fees were ended in participating schools from 1967 along with free school transport. The school-leaving age was raised from 14 to 15 in 1972.",
