    "marks": 30,
    "model": "John Charles McQuaid was born in Cootehill, Co. Cavan, in 1895 and became Archbishop of Dublin in 1940. During the Mother and Child crisis of 1951 he advised the government that the scheme conflicted with Catholic teaching on the family. He attended Vatican II and reassured Dubliners that the council would not disturb their faith, although he was wary of ecumenism. He founded the Catholic Social Service Conference and helped build schools and churches in the Dublin suburbs.",
