    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Sylvia Meehan was born in Dublin in 1929 and worked as a teacher, becoming vice-president of the Association of Secondary Teachers, Ireland. She chaired the women's committee of the Irish Congress of Trade Unions. She became the first chairperson of the Employment Equality Agency in 1977, a post she held until 1992. The Agency's research on girls and women in education, pay, maternity leave and childcare helped shape later legislation.",
