    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Bolsheviks seized power in October 1917, and Lenin led them from 1903 to 1924 and headed the first Soviet government. During the civil war the Cheka used terror against opponents, War Communism requisitioned grain, and rival parties were banned. Lenin crushed the Kronstadt revolt in March 1921 and introduced the New Economic Policy, which allowed small private trade and peasant sales of surplus grain. The USSR was formally created in December 1922, and Lenin died in January 1924, leaving the party without a clear successor.",
