    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Lateran Treaties of 11 February 1929 ended the long dispute between the Italian state and the papacy and created the independent state of Vatican City. Catholicism was recognised as the sole religion of the Italian state, and the Church received 1.75 billion lire in compensation for the lost papal states. In 1931 the regime clashed with Catholic Action over its youth groups, and Pope Pius XI protested in the encyclical Non abbiamo bisogno. The racial laws of 1938 caused tension, but the Church opposed them only in part and never broke with the regime.",
