    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Bing Crosby was an American singer and actor whose radio shows, records and films made him the most popular entertainer of his age. In the early 1930s he became a radio singer and developed a relaxed crooning style suited to the microphone. He starred in films including the Road series with Bob Hope from 1940, and he won the Academy Award for Best Actor for Going My Way. His recording of White Christmas, released in 1942, became one of the best-selling songs of all time and was hugely popular with troops. He entertained Allied troops through radio broadcasts and USO tours, including a tour of Britain and France in 1944. His music spread the sounds of American radio into Europe.",
