    "model": "Churchill's refusal to negotiate a peace in 1940 kept Britain fighting and opened a base from which the Allies could later invade Europe. His speeches, including blood, toil, tears and sweat, sustained morale after Dunkirk and during the Blitz. Operation Dynamo evacuated over 330,000 Allied troops from Dunkirk between 26 May and 4 June 1940. He formed a coalition with Labour leaders Attlee and Bevin, and he also acted as Minister of Defence. He built a close relationship with Roosevelt and worked with Roosevelt and Stalin at the Tehran and Yalta conferences. Historians criticise the bombing of Dresden and the diversion of forces to Greece in 1941, but British strategy relied heavily on American resources after 1941.",
