    "model": "Thatcher became Conservative leader in February 1975 and Prime Minister in May 1979, and she won the general elections of 1979, 1983 and 1987. Her government pursued monetarism, cut public spending and reduced the power of the trade unions through laws passed in 1980, 1982 and 1984. Britain's victory in the Falklands War in June 1982 helped her re-election in 1983. Her negotiation of the Fontainebleau rebate in 1984 reduced Britain's net contribution to the EEC budget, and her Bruges speech of 1988 criticised federal Europe. She resigned as Prime Minister in November 1990.",
