    "label": "C4",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "A strength of Ho Chi Minh was that he founded the Viet Minh in 1941 to unite communists and non-communist nationalists against the Japanese and the French. His proclamation of the Democratic Republic of Vietnam on 2 September 1945, which quoted the American Declaration of Independence, gave his cause a powerful nationalist appeal. He led the government through the First Indochina War, and with Vo Nguyen Giap the Viet Minh defeated the French at Dien Bien Phu in 1954. A weakness was that the Geneva Accords of 1954 divided Vietnam, and his government did not control the whole country until 1975. His land reform of 1953 to 1956 was violent, and he was forced to admit his errors publicly. He depended heavily on Soviet and Chinese aid, and Western governments saw him as a communist agitator.",
