    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Nixon's policy of Vietnamisation, which followed the Nixon Doctrine announced at Guam in July 1969, cut US troop numbers from about 540,000 in 1969 to under 30,000 by late 1972. The Paris Peace Accords were signed on 27 January 1973, and the last US combat troops left Vietnam by late March 1973. Congress passed the Case-Church amendment, which cut off funds for US combat in Indochina from 15 August 1973. North Vietnam's 1975 offensive overran South Vietnam, and the capture of Saigon on 30 April 1975 ended the war.",
