    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The National Health Service began in Northern Ireland on 5 July 1948, the same day as in England, Scotland and Wales. National Insurance, unemployment benefit and pensions were run on a UK-wide basis, and the Social Services Agreement of 1949 formalised parity, with the British Treasury meeting much of the cost. The Education Act (Northern Ireland) 1947 provided free secondary education, although pupils were sorted by the eleven-plus examination. The Northern Ireland Housing Trust, set up in 1945, built homes across the province, but welfare parity did not remove discrimination in council house allocation and jobs.",
