    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Health Act 1953 replaced the Mother and Child Scheme with means-tested maternity, child and hospital care. The Voluntary Health Insurance Board was set up in 1957 to offer private health insurance to people who earned too much for free hospital care. The Health Act 1970 created eight regional health boards, which began work in 1971 and took over the functions of the old county health authorities. Contributory old age pensions were introduced in 1961, and pay-related benefit for unemployed and sick workers followed in 1974.",
