    "model": "Lemass was a founder of Fianna Fáil in 1926 and the architect of its protectionist industrial policy of the 1930s. As Taoiseach from June 1959 he carried through the First Programme for Economic Expansion, which set growth targets for 1959 to 1963. He applied for Ireland to join the EEC on 31 July 1961 to secure access to larger European markets. He signed the Anglo-Irish Free Trade Agreement in December 1965, which removed tariffs on trade with Britain over ten years.",
