    "model": "The 1937 Constitution made Irish the national and first official language, and it was a compulsory school subject that had to be passed for the Leaving Certificate. Gael Linn, founded in 1953, promoted Irish through records, newsreels and the 1959 film Mise Éire. Raidió na Gaeltachta began broadcasting from Connemara on 2 April 1972, giving Irish speakers a regular service. In 1973 the government ended the rule that students must pass Irish to gain the Leaving Certificate, but the number of everyday speakers kept falling outside the Gaeltacht.",
