    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Sir Robert Peel was Conservative Prime Minister in 1834 to 1835 and again from 1841 to 1846. As Home Secretary he founded the Metropolitan Police in London in 1829. He reintroduced income tax in 1842 to pay for cuts in tariffs on many imports. The Bank Charter Act of 1844 regulated banknote issue by the Bank of England. He repealed the Corn Laws in 1846, which split the Conservative Party, and he resigned that June.",
