    "model": "Feargus O'Connor was born in Co. Cork in 1796 and trained as a barrister. He founded the Northern Star newspaper in Leeds in 1837, which became the most widely read radical paper in Britain. He was a leading figure in the National Charter Association and took part in the Chartist campaigns of 1839, 1842 and 1848. He was imprisoned for seditious libel in 1840 to 1841 and was elected MP for Nottingham in 1847. His National Land Company collapsed after financial mismanagement, and his breakdown in 1852 ended his influence.",
