    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Balkan nationalism threatened the Ottoman Empire and invited Russian and Austrian intervention. Serbia gained autonomy under Miloš Obrenović after the second rising of 1815, which the Sultan recognised in 1830. The Greek rising of 1821 won European sympathy, and Byron died at Missolonghi in 1824. The battle of Navarino in 1827 destroyed the Ottoman and Egyptian fleet and made Greek independence possible. The London Protocol of 1830 recognised an independent Greece, which was made a monarchy under Otto in 1832.",
