    "model": "Bing Crosby, born in Tacoma in 1903, became a radio singer in the early 1930s and developed a relaxed crooning style. He starred in films including the Road series with Bob Hope, and he won the Academy Award for Best Actor for Going My Way. His recording of White Christmas, released in 1942, became one of the best-selling songs of all time and was hugely popular with troops. He entertained Allied troops through radio broadcasts and USO tours, and his music spread American radio sounds into Europe.",
