    "label": "C3",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Each rally was held in September at Nuremberg and lasted about a week, with set days for the party leadership, the Labour Service, the Hitler Youth, the SA and SS and, from 1935, the armed forces. In 1934 Hitler walked between ranks of SA and SS men at the Luitpold Arena to lay a wreath, and the Labour Service marched with spades. The rallies consecrated party flags with the Blood Flag, and Hitler's night speeches set out party doctrine and foreign policy. The 1933 rally was the Rally of Victory, the 1935 rally announced the Nuremberg Laws, and the 1938 rally celebrated the Anschluss. The rallies also had popular elements such as special trains and free food, and the 1936 rally announced the Four Year Plan. The 1939 rally was cancelled at the outbreak of war.",
