    "label": "C4",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Stalin chaired the State Defence Committee from 30 June 1941 and became Supreme Commander in August 1941. Factories were moved east to the Urals and Siberia in 1941, and tank and aircraft output rose sharply by 1942. Lend-Lease supplies from Britain and the United States, including trucks and food, supported the Red Army from 1941. The Soviet victory at Stalingrad from August 1942 to February 1943 turned the war, and the Red Army reached Berlin in April and May 1945. Stalin used the NKVD and Order 227 of July 1942, Not one step back, to enforce discipline, with blocking detachments and penal battalions. The war cost about 27 million Soviet lives, but Stalin's authority was strengthened and he was given the rank of Generalissimo in 1945.",
