    "model": "The transistor, invented at Bell Laboratories in December 1947, replaced vacuum tubes in computers and made them smaller and cheaper. Computers automated routine office and factory work, which reduced demand for some clerical and manufacturing jobs in Western Europe, while service jobs in banking and insurance grew. The IBM Personal Computer of 12 August 1981 spread computing into offices and homes during the 1980s. Tim Berners-Lee proposed the World Wide Web at CERN in 1989, and it was launched publicly in 1991, which transformed communication and access to information.",
