    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Britain referred the Palestine question to the United Nations in February 1947, and the UN General Assembly passed Resolution 181 on 29 November 1947 to partition Palestine into Arab and Jewish states. Britain refused to implement partition itself and said it would withdraw by 15 May 1948, and the Mandate expired on 14 May 1948, the day Israel was proclaimed. The declaration of Israel led to war with the neighbouring Arab states, and about 700,000 Palestinian Arabs fled or were expelled from territory that became Israel. The armistice agreements of 1949 left Israel with more territory than the UN plan had allotted it, and the refugee question and hostility between Israel and its neighbours remained unresolved.",
