    "label": "B3",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Born Nguyen Sinh Cung in 1890 in central Vietnam, Ho Chi Minh spent about thirty years abroad, including in France and the Soviet Union, before returning in 1941 to found the Viet Minh. He joined the French Communist Party in 1920 and helped found the Indochinese Communist Party in 1930. He proclaimed the Democratic Republic of Vietnam in Hanoi on 2 September 1945 and led the government through the war against France. The Viet Minh defeated the French at Dien Bien Phu in May 1954, and the Geneva Accords divided Vietnam at the 17th parallel.",
