    "label": "B4",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Algeria became independent on 5 July 1962 under the Évian Accords, which had given France access to Saharan oil and gas and use of the Mers-el-Kébir naval base for a time. In 1968 France handed over Mers-el-Kébir, and in 1971 Algeria nationalised French oil and gas holdings. About 800,000 settlers left Algeria in 1962, mostly for France, and the harkis who had served in the French army were largely left behind, with tens of thousands killed in reprisals. President Chirac paid national tribute to the harkis in 2001, and President Macron asked for their forgiveness in 2021.",
