    "model": "In August 1964 Johnson used the Gulf of Tonkin Resolution, passed by 416 votes to 0 in the House and 88 to 2 in the Senate, to take wide war powers. He presented himself in the 1964 election as the candidate of restraint while privately preparing for a larger war. In 1965 he ordered Operation Rolling Thunder, a sustained bombing of North Vietnam beginning on 2 March 1965, and the first US Marine combat units landed at Da Nang on 8 March. On 28 July 1965 he announced that US forces would rise from 75,000 to 125,000 without asking Congress for a declaration of war. Westmoreland's strategy of search and destroy, measured by the body count, pushed US troop numbers to over 500,000 by 1968. In March 1968 he announced a partial halt to the bombing, offered peace talks and declared that he would not seek re-election.",
