    "label": "2(a)",
    "marks": 10,
    "model": "Yes, both documents agree that the appeal of Hitler himself was greater than the appeal of his ideas.\nDocument A says there was little enthusiasm for the doctrines of National Socialism but a fanatical devotion to Hitler, whom the writer describes as the Messiah sent to redeem the German people.\nDocument B says the appeal of Hitler himself was far more powerful than the appeal of his doctrine, and shows it in the crowd's cheers, frenzy and tears.",
