    "model": "Ian Paisley was born in Armagh in 1926 and founded the Free Presbyterian Church in 1951. From 1966 he led the 'O'Neill must go' campaign against the Prime Minister's reforms, and he was jailed for three months that year. He won the Bannside seat at Stormont in April 1970 and founded the Democratic Unionist Party in 1971, which he led until 2008. He opposed the Sunningdale Agreement, supported the 1974 strike and led protests against the Anglo-Irish Agreement.",
