    "model": "Rupert Brooke's 1914 sonnets expressed patriotic idealism about dying for England, and he was celebrated as a hero after he died of blood poisoning on the way to Gallipoli in April 1915. Siegfried Sassoon published a statement condemning the war in July 1917 and was sent to Craiglockhart instead of facing a court martial. Henri Barbusse's novel Le Feu (1916) described the lives of French infantry in the trenches and won the Prix Goncourt. Erich Maria Remarque's All Quiet on the Western Front (1929) showed young soldiers ruined by war and shaped later memory of the conflict.",
