    "model": "Truman authorised the atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki in August 1945, and he met Stalin for the first time at the Potsdam conference that summer. He announced the Truman Doctrine on 12 March 1947, committing the United States to support free peoples resisting communist pressure, and asked Congress for about 400 million dollars for Greece and Turkey. The Marshall Plan, passed in April 1948, gave about 13 billion dollars of aid to Western Europe to rebuild its economies. He backed the North Atlantic Treaty, signed on 4 April 1949, whose Article 5 treated an attack on one member as an attack on all. He answered the Berlin blockade of June 1948 with an airlift that lasted until May 1949. When North Korea invaded the South in June 1950, he sent US forces without a congressional vote, and he dismissed MacArthur in April 1951 after the general publicly argued for attacking China.",
