    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Margaret Thatcher was Prime Minister from May 1979 to November 1990, and she made security and the defeat of terrorism central to her policy in Northern Ireland. She refused to grant political status to the hunger strikers in 1981, saying that crime is crime is crime, and ten hunger strikers died. She signed the Anglo-Irish Agreement with Garret FitzGerald at Hillsborough Castle on 15 November 1985, giving the Irish government a formal consultative role. On 12 October 1984 the IRA bombed the Grand Hotel in Brighton during the Conservative Party conference, and Thatcher escaped, though five people were killed.",
