    "label": "B4",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Gerry Adams was born in Belfast in 1948 into a republican family in West Belfast, and he was interned in the early 1970s. He was elected president of Sinn Féin in November 1983, and he led the party into electoral politics. In June 1983 he had won the West Belfast seat at Westminster, which Sinn Féin members refused to take up. He took part in the dialogue with the SDLP's John Hume from 1988, and again from 1991 to 1993. Supporters credit him with leading republicans from armed struggle towards negotiation.",
