    "model": "The Health Act 1953 replaced the Mother and Child Scheme with means-tested maternity and child services. The Health Act 1970 created eight regional health boards, which began work in 1971 and took over the old county health authorities. The Social Welfare Act 1952 brought the existing insurance schemes into a single system, and contributory old age pensions were added in 1961. Unmarried mother's allowance was introduced in 1973, and pay-related benefit for unemployed and sick workers followed in 1974. Medical cards gave lower-income families free GP care and medicines.",
