    "label": "C3",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Breandán Ó hEithir was a writer, journalist and broadcaster who worked in both Irish and English. He was a journalist and broadcaster with RTÉ, reporting on current affairs, culture and sport, and he wrote a regular newspaper column. His novel Lig Sinn i gCathú, published in 1976, satirised the life of a Galway student and was widely read in Irish. He translated it as Lead Us into Temptation in 1978, bringing it to English readers. Over the Bar, published in 1984, was a personal history of the GAA. The Begrudger's Guide to Irish Politics, published in 1986, gave a witty account of political life in English, and showed that Irish could be a living language for modern subjects.",
