    "marks": 30,
    "model": "In Serbia, Karadjordje led the First Serbian Uprising from 1804, and Miloš Obrenović led a second rising in 1815 that negotiated autonomy, recognised by the Sultan in 1830. The Greek War of Independence began in the Peloponnese in March 1821, and an assembly at Epidaurus declared independence in January 1822. The British, French and Russian fleets destroyed the Ottoman and Egyptian fleet at Navarino in 1827, which made Greek independence possible. By 1832 Greece had been made a monarchy under Otto of Bavaria.",
