    "model": "Karol Wojtyla was born in Wadowice in 1920, became Archbishop of Krakow, and was elected pope on 16 October 1978, the first non-Italian pope since 1523. He took part in the Second Vatican Council, where he helped to draft Gaudium et Spes. His visit to Poland from 2 to 10 June 1979 drew huge crowds and encouraged Poles to organise independently of the state. He was shot in St Peter's Square on 13 May 1981 by Mehmet Ali Agca, and he visited his attacker in prison in December 1983. He gave moral support to Solidarity, meeting Lech Walesa during his 1983 visit to Poland. He travelled more than any previous pope, visited Ireland in 1979, and received Gorbachev at the Vatican on 1 December 1989.",
