    "label": "B4",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Edward Carson was born in Dublin in 1854 and educated at Trinity College, where he became a leading barrister. He was Solicitor General for Ireland in 1892 and Solicitor General for England from 1900 to 1906. He became MP for Dublin University in 1892 and in 1895 cross-examined Oscar Wilde in the libel case that ruined him. In 1910 he became leader of the Irish Unionist parliamentary party.",
