    "model": "The GAA was founded at Hayes's Hotel in Thurles in 1884 to promote Gaelic football, hurling and athletics as a distinctly Irish sporting culture. Irish-American clubs playing Gaelic games appeared in New York, Chicago and Boston, and New York became the GAA's main centre in North America. Gaelic Park in the Bronx opened in 1926 and gave emigrants a home for their games. A London GAA board was set up in the 1890s, and clubs in Britain and Australia gave emigrants a regular social life built around their Irish identity.",
