    "model": "Daniel Mannix was born in Charleville, Co. Cork, in 1864, and he was president of Maynooth College from 1903 until 1912. He became coadjutor archbishop of Melbourne in 1912 and archbishop in 1917. He led the campaign against conscription in Australia, and the conscription referendums of 1916 and 1917 were both defeated. In August 1920 a British naval vessel took him off his ship at sea and landed him in England, and he was banned from entering Ireland.",
