    "marks": 30,
    "model": "After 1945 the mission opened new parishes, schools, hospitals and training colleges across south-eastern Nigeria. The Archdiocese of Onitsha was created in 1950 with the Irish Spiritan Charles Heerey as archbishop, and Joseph Whelan became the first bishop of Owerri. Mission schools became the main route to education in the region, and the Catholic mission ran a large share of primary and secondary schools. Hospitals and dispensaries run by the Holy Rosary Sisters and the Medical Missionaries of Mary provided care in rural areas where government services were few.",
