    "label": "B4",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Kennedy's great-grandfather Patrick Kennedy left Dunganstown, Co. Wexford, in 1849, so the family's Irish origins were well known in Ireland. Kennedy was elected president in 1960 as the first Catholic president of the United States, and many Irish Americans saw his election as acceptance of Irish Catholics in public life. He visited Ireland from 26 to 29 June 1963 and addressed the Oireachtas in Dublin on 28 June. His assassination on 22 November 1963 was mourned widely in Ireland, and his portrait hung in many Irish homes.",
    "model_source": "haiku",
    "answerStatus": "written",
