    "model": "The welfare reforms of the 1940s were extended to Northern Ireland on the principle of parity with Britain. National Insurance, unemployment benefit and pensions were run on a UK-wide basis, and the Social Services Agreement of 1949 formalised parity with Britain paying much of the cost. The NHS began on 5 July 1948, and the Education Act of 1947 provided free secondary education for all pupils. Discrimination nevertheless continued, as unionist-controlled councils favoured Protestants in housing and Catholics were under-represented in jobs and the RUC.",
