    "model": "The Downing Street Declaration was issued on 15 December 1993 by John Major and Albert Reynolds. It stated that the British government had no selfish strategic or economic interest in Northern Ireland. It said a united Ireland would require the consent of a majority in Northern Ireland, and that Britain would legislate for it if a majority wished. It invited republicans to renounce violence and join talks, and the Irish government agreed to examine Articles 2 and 3 of its constitution.",
