    "label": "B3",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Marx was born in Trier in 1818 and became editor of the Rheinische Zeitung in Cologne in 1842. He was expelled from Paris in 1845 and from Prussia in 1849, and he settled in London, where he lived until his death in 1883. He held that class struggle drives history and that capitalism would be overthrown by the working class. The first volume of Das Kapital appeared in 1867, analysing how capitalists profit from the surplus value produced by labour.",
