    "label": "C4",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Mazzini founded Young Italy at Marseille in 1831 to campaign for an independent, united Italian republic through popular insurrection. He planned risings and sent agents into Italy, and his ideas inspired ordinary followers. In 1834 he founded Young Europe to link revolutionary movements across the continent. In 1849 he was one of the three triumvirs who governed the Roman Republic, and Garibaldi commanded its defence. The National Society of 1857, founded by Manin, La Farina and Garibaldi, backed Piedmont's leadership in place of Mazzini's republicanism. Mazzini's conspiracies largely failed, but historians see him as a key ideologue whose ideas shaped the Risorgimento.",
