    "label": "B4",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Rosa Luxemburg helped found the Communist Party of Germany (KPD) around 30 December 1918, with others from the Spartacus League. She wanted a council republic on the Russian model, while the SPD leaders wanted an elected parliament. During the Spartacist rising of January 1919 radicals occupied newspaper buildings in Berlin, but the defence minister Gustav Noske crushed the revolt with regular troops and Freikorps, volunteer units of ex-soldiers. Luxemburg and Liebknecht were arrested and murdered by Freikorps officers on 15 January 1919, three days after the rising ended.",
