    "model": "Marshall Aid was announced by the US Secretary of State, George Marshall, in a speech at Harvard on 5 June 1947. The USA gave about 13 billion dollars, mostly as grants, through the European Recovery Programme from 1948 to 1952. Sixteen European countries shared the aid, which was coordinated by the Organisation for European Economic Co-operation, set up in 1948. The USA wanted to stop economic collapse from helping communist parties, especially in France and Italy, and the Soviet Union would not let eastern European states take part.",
