    "model": "Jean Monnet produced the Monnet Plan for modernising French industry through state investment after 1946. He drafted the Schuman Declaration of 9 May 1950, which proposed pooling French and West German coal and steel under a joint authority. As first president of the High Authority of the European Coal and Steel Community from 1952 to 1955, he helped create the first supranational community. Delors, president of the European Commission from 1985 to 1995, drove the Single European Act of 1986, which set a 1992 deadline for completing a single market. His 1989 committee report set out a three-stage route to economic and monetary union, which became the basis of the Maastricht Treaty. Delors also took part in the Maastricht negotiations of 1991, which created the European Union and committed member states to a single currency.",
    "model_source": "haiku",
