    "label": "B2",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Katanga was the richest mining region of the Belgian Congo, and its copper, cobalt and uranium were run by the Belgian company Union Minière du Haut-Katanga. Tshombe proclaimed the secession of Katanga on 11 July 1960, eleven days after independence, with support from Belgian officers and foreign mercenaries who led the Katanga Gendarmerie. The UN Security Council authorised the ONUC operation, and UN troops entered Katanga on 12 August 1960. Resolution 169 of November 1961 explicitly authorised action against the secession, and the UN's operations continued until Tshombe announced the end of the secession at Kolwezi on 14 January 1963.",
