    "label": "C4",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Ho Chi Minh was a very successful nationalist leader, though his success was incomplete in his lifetime. Born Nguyen Sinh Cung in 1890, he spent about thirty years abroad and joined the French Communist Party in 1920. In 1919 he petitioned the Versailles peace conference for Vietnamese rights, but the Allies ignored it. He founded the Viet Minh in May 1941, uniting communists and non-communist nationalists against the Japanese and then the French. On 2 September 1945 he proclaimed the Democratic Republic of Vietnam in Hanoi, quoting the American Declaration of Independence. Under his leadership the Viet Minh, with Vo Nguyen Giap as its general, defeated France at Dien Bien Phu in 1954. However, the Geneva Accords divided Vietnam at the 17th parallel, so he ruled only the North, and he died in 1969 before Vietnam was reunified in 1975.",
