    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Representation of the People Act 1918 gave the vote to men over 21 and women over 30, roughly tripling the Irish electorate. Sinn Féin won 73 of Ireland's 105 seats in the election held on 14 December 1918, while the Irish Parliamentary Party won only six and the Unionists won 26. Sinn Féin took about 47 per cent of the votes, and many of its successful candidates were in prison. Markievicz became the first woman elected to the House of Commons but did not take her seat.",
