    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Anglo-Irish Agreement was signed on 15 November 1985 at Hillsborough Castle by Margaret Thatcher and Garret FitzGerald. It set up an Intergovernmental Conference with a permanent secretariat at Maryfield, through which the Irish government could put forward views on Northern Ireland. It gave the Irish government only a consultative role, and affirmed that Northern Ireland's status would not change without majority consent. Unionists responded with the slogan 'Ulster says No' and a large rally at Belfast City Hall, and fifteen unionist MPs resigned their seats in January 1986.",
