    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Seamus Heaney was born in 1939 at Mossbawn, County Derry, and became the leading poet of the Troubles. His collection North, published in 1975, used Iron Age bog bodies to reflect on ritual killing in Northern Ireland. His later collections Field Work in 1979 and Station Island in 1984 continued his engagement with violence, memory and the Catholic tradition. Historians see his work as giving expression to grief, guilt and the search for an identity beyond sectarianism.",
