    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Metternich was Austrian foreign minister from 1809 and state chancellor from 1821, and he dominated the Congress of Vienna in 1814 and 1815. He drafted the Carlsbad Decrees of 1819, which banned the Burschenschaften, put the universities under government supervisors and imposed press censorship. At the congresses of Troppau and Laibach he justified intervention against revolutions, and Austrian troops crushed the revolutions in Naples and Piedmont. The Six Articles of 1832, passed after the Hambach Festival, reasserted the authority of the princes over the German states.",
