    "model": "Friedrich Krupp founded a cast steel works at Essen in 1811, and his son Alfred moved it into breech-loading guns that Prussia adopted in the 1860s. Alfred provided housing, schools and pension funds for workers, a paternalism that demanded loyalty and discouraged politics. Friedrich Alfred Krupp took over in 1887 and expanded into naval armour plate and shipbuilding, with the Kaiser as a close friend and the fleet a large customer. In 1902 his daughter Bertha inherited the firm at 16, and in 1914 it produced the 42 cm 'Big Bertha' howitzer used at Liège and Namur.",
