    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Lenin led the Bolsheviks in seizing power in October 1917 and presided over the Council of People's Commissars, the first Soviet government. During the civil war he authorised terror, and the Bolsheviks banned rival parties so that the Communist Party became the only legal party. At the Tenth Party Congress in March 1921 he adopted the New Economic Policy, which allowed small private trade and peasant sales of surplus grain. He suppressed the Kronstadt revolt of March 1921, in which sailors had demanded free elections. Lenin died on 21 January 1924, leaving the party without a clear successor.",
