    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Lateran Treaties of 11 February 1929 ended the dispute between the Italian state and the papacy and created the Vatican City state. Under the treaties Catholicism became the sole religion of the Italian state, religious marriage was given civil effect, and the Church received compensation of 1.75 billion lire. Mussolini gained the support of the Catholic majority, and the Church won religious teaching in state schools in return. In 1931 the regime clashed with Catholic Action over its youth groups, and Pius XI protested in the encyclical Non abbiamo bisogno, although he rarely challenged Mussolini openly.",
