    "marks": 30,
    "model": "After the armistice of 22 June 1940 France was divided into an occupied zone and an unoccupied zone, and on 10 July 1940 the National Assembly voted full powers to Marshal Pétain, which ended the Third Republic. The Vichy regime rejected republican values, replaced the motto Liberté, Égalité, Fraternité with Travail, Famille, Patrie, and promoted the National Revolution of authoritarian conservatism. Vichy passed anti-Jewish laws without German demand, and in July 1942 French police arrested about 13,000 Jews in Paris. The Milice, founded in January 1943, hunted members of the Resistance, and German troops occupied the whole country in November 1942.",
