    "label": "B2",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Achmad Sukarno founded the Indonesian Nationalist Party in 1927 and was imprisoned by the Dutch in 1929. With Hatta he proclaimed Indonesian independence in Jakarta on 17 August 1945, and he became the first president of the Republic. He introduced Guided Democracy by decree on 5 July 1959, which ended parliamentary government and gave power to the president, the army and a National Front. Economic decline and the Konfrontasi campaign against Malaysia weakened his position, and the Supersemar order of 11 March 1966 stripped him of real power.",
