    "label": "B4",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Born Nguyen Sinh Cung in 1890, Ho Chi Minh spent about thirty years abroad and joined the French Communist Party in 1920. In 1919 he presented a petition for Vietnamese rights to the Versailles peace conference, which the Allies ignored. He founded the Viet Minh in 1941 and proclaimed the Democratic Republic of Vietnam in Hanoi on 2 September 1945. He led the war against France, and he headed the North after the division of Vietnam in 1954, dying in September 1969 before the war ended.",
