    "model": "Joseph McCarthy, a Republican senator from Wisconsin, rose to national prominence with his Wheeling speech of 9 February 1950, claiming to hold a list of communists in the State Department. His methods of guilt by association, unnamed lists and personal smears led critics to coin the term McCarthyism in 1950. Edward R. Murrow's See It Now programme of 9 March 1954 used McCarthy's own words and film to criticise him. The televised Army-McCarthy hearings of 1954 turned opinion against him, and the Senate censured him on 2 December 1954.",
