    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Chicano movement, led in part by Cesar Chavez, organised farm workers in California from the early 1960s, and the Delano grape strike won national support. The American Indian Movement was founded in Minneapolis in 1968 to campaign against discrimination and for treaty rights. The Immigration Act of 1965 and the Bilingual Education Act of 1968 encouraged a more diverse society. The Stonewall riots of June 1969 began the modern gay rights movement after police raided a gay bar in Greenwich Village.",
