    "model": "Yes, I can see why Fulbright was an effective critic.\nHe raised a wide range of problems, including the Vietnam War and the Great Society reforms.\nHe showed how the war left the President and Congress unable to tend to social problems.\nHe used strong language, such as 'sickened' and 'violence and undisciplined power', which drew attention and controversy.\nHe stressed the urgency of problems such as exploding cities.\nHowever, the extract offers no solutions, which weakens his effectiveness as a critic, and he was probably disliked by President Johnson.",
