    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Isaac Butt, a Protestant barrister and former Conservative MP, founded the Home Government Association in Dublin in May 1870. His programme was federal Home Rule, with an Irish parliament dealing with domestic affairs while Westminster kept control of defence and foreign policy. In the 1874 election Home Rulers won about 60 of the 103 Irish seats, but Butt could not make the party effective. He relied on constitutional methods such as persuasion and parliamentary motions, and by the time of his death in 1879 his control had slipped to the obstructionists.",
