    "model": "The GAA was founded at Hayes' Hotel in Thurles on 1 November 1884, with Maurice Davin elected as president and Michael Cusack as one of the secretaries. Archbishop Thomas Croke of Cashel agreed to be patron in a letter of December 1884 that urged the revival of Irish sports as an act of national self-respect. In 1885 Davin drew up the first rules for hurling and Gaelic football, and the association banned members from playing foreign games such as cricket, rugby and soccer. The first All-Ireland championships began in 1887, and the first hurling final was played at Birr on 1 April 1888.",
