    "model": "Edward Harland bought a small yard on Queen's Island in 1858, and in 1861 he went into partnership with Gustav Wolff, a German-born engineer. William Pirrie, born in Quebec to Ulster parents, became a partner in 1874 and chairman after Harland's death in 1895. Workman Clark, founded in 1880 by Frank Workman and George Clark, became Belfast's second great shipyard and built cargo and passenger ships. The Arrol Gantry, built in 1908 and 1909, allowed the liners Olympic and Titanic to be built side by side.",
