    "label": "B4",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Edward Carson, a Dublin-born barrister, became Solicitor General for Ireland in 1892 and was MP for Dublin University from the same year. In 1910 he became leader of the Irish Unionist parliamentary party, and he was the chief unionist campaigner against Home Rule from 1911 to 1914. He led the Ulster Day rally on 28 September 1912, when about 237,000 men signed the Solemn League and Covenant. In September 1913 he was chosen to chair a planned Provisional Government of Ulster, which would take over if Home Rule became law.",
