    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Griffith founded the newspaper United Irishman and, in 1905, Sinn Féin, advocating a dual monarchy and economic self-reliance. He was interned after the Easter Rising, though he had not taken part in it, and he stepped aside for de Valera as Sinn Féin president in 1917. As Minister for Foreign Affairs he led the Treaty negotiations in London as chairman of the Irish delegation, and he signed the Treaty on 6 December 1921. He was elected President of the Dáil in January 1922 and led the pro-Treaty side until his death from a cerebral haemorrhage on 12 August 1922.",
