    "label": "B4",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Cosgrave's governments used the Imperial Conferences, and the Balfour Declaration of 1926 described Britain and the dominions as autonomous communities, equal in status. The Statute of Westminster of 1931 gave the dominions legislative independence, which de Valera later used to change the Treaty. De Valera removed the oath in 1933, ended appeals to the Privy Council in the same year, and removed the Crown from the Constitution in December 1936. The Anglo-Irish Agreements of April 1938 returned the Treaty ports and ended the Economic War, and the Republic of Ireland Act of 1948 left the Commonwealth in 1949.",
