    "label": "B3",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Downing Street Declaration of 15 December 1993 was issued by Prime Minister John Major and Taoiseach Albert Reynolds. It said the Irish people as a whole had the right to self-determination, exercised by agreement between North and South. It stated that Britain had no selfish strategic or economic interest in Northern Ireland and would legislate for a united Ireland if a majority wished it. It invited republicans to renounce violence and join talks, and it committed the Irish government to examine Articles 2 and 3 of its constitution.",
