    "label": "B4",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Breandán Ó hEithir was born on Inis Mór in the Aran Islands on 18 January 1930 and became a writer, journalist and broadcaster. His satirical novel Lig Sinn i gCathú, published in 1976 about the life of a Galway student, was widely read in Irish. He translated it himself as Lead Us into Temptation in 1978. Over the Bar, published in 1984, was a personal history of the GAA. The Begrudger's Guide to Irish Politics, published in 1986, was a witty account of political life written in English.",
