    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Peel founded the Metropolitan Police in London as Home Secretary in 1829, creating a professional force that became a model for others. He conceded Catholic emancipation in 1829 with the Duke of Wellington to avoid civil conflict in Ireland, which angered many Tories. The Tamworth Manifesto of December 1834 set out a moderate programme of reform within the Conservative tradition, which became the basis of the modern Conservative Party. He reintroduced income tax in 1842 to pay for tariff reductions, and in 1846 he repealed the Corn Laws.",
