    "label": "C3",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Woodrow Wilson kept the USA neutral from 1914 until he asked Congress on 2 April 1917 to declare war so that the world might be made safe for democracy. On 8 January 1918 he announced the Fourteen Points as American war aims, including self-determination, open covenants of peace and free trade. Germany's armistice request of October 1918 relied on these points, and Britain and France agreed to them as a basis in November. At Paris he insisted that the League Covenant be part of the treaty, but he compromised on reparations, Article 231 and the Saar to win agreement. The Republican Senate, led by Henry Cabot Lodge, rejected the treaty in November 1919 and March 1920, so the USA never joined the League of Nations. His stroke in October 1919 left him incapacitated for the rest of his term.",
