    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Mussolini founded the Fasci di Combattimento in Milan in March 1919, and his armed squadristi attacked socialist and Catholic organisations between 1920 and 1922. King Victor Emmanuel III refused to sign a state of siege during the March on Rome, and Mussolini took office as Prime Minister on 30 October 1922. After the murder of Matteotti in 1924, Mussolini accepted political responsibility for the violence in January 1925, which marked the start of his open dictatorship. The Leggi Fascistissime of 1925 to 1926 made him responsible only to the King and let him rule by decree. In 1936 he announced the Rome-Berlin Axis, and in 1939 he signed the Pact of Steel with Germany.",
