    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Rationing of bacon, butter and sugar began in January 1940, and the Ministry of Food under Lord Woolton organised the supply of basic foods such as the National Loaf. Operation Pied Piper moved about 1.5 million people, most of them children, from British cities to the countryside in the first days of September 1939. The Blitz began on 7 September 1940 and killed about 40,000 civilians in Britain, while Anderson and Morrison shelters protected many households. Women took war work in factories, the armed services and civil defence, and the Beveridge Report of 1942 proposed a welfare state.",
