    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Radar gave Britain early warning of air attacks through the Chain Home system, and later airborne and ship-borne radar helped locate U-boats and aircraft. At Bletchley Park British codebreakers decrypted German Enigma messages, and the resulting Ultra intelligence guided operations in the Battle of the Atlantic and the North African campaign. Strategic bombing by RAF Bomber Command and the US Army Air Forces attacked German cities, causing fires and civilian deaths in raids such as Hamburg in July 1943. German Panzer divisions combined armour with motorised infantry and used radio communication to co-ordinate attacks. The atomic bombs dropped on Hiroshima on 6 August 1945 and Nagasaki on 9 August 1945 ended the war against Japan.",
