    "model": "The Lome Conventions were trade and aid agreements between the European Economic Community and the African, Caribbean and Pacific states, beginning with Lome I, which was signed on 28 February 1975 with 46 states. Lome I gave ACP exports largely duty-free access to European markets without requiring reciprocal concessions, which was a new departure in trade relations. STABEX compensated ACP countries when earnings from specified agricultural exports fell below a set level. The later Conventions of 1979, 1984 and 1989 added conditions on human rights and governance before the Cotonou Agreement replaced them in 2000.",
