    "label": "2(a)",
    "marks": 10,
    "model": "Yes, both documents show that opponents of the boycott used violence against its supporters.\nDocument A says bombings were added to threats, with the homes of Rev. King and E.D. Nixon bombed and crosses burned by the Ku Klux Klan.\nDocument B refers to continued threats and violence, including the bombing of homes and the hanging in effigy of a Black man and a white man who supported integration.\nDocument B also says the Ku Klux Klan was allowed to demonstrate without police interference.",
