    "label": "2(b)",
    "marks": 10,
    "model": "Document B tells us more about the role of the Montgomery police during the boycott.\nDocument A says the police were told to break up the car pools by enforcing traffic regulations, and that people assembled for car pools were to be charged with loitering.\nDocument B says mass arrests were authorised by officials, and that the city police led the procession where effigies were hanged, yet no arrests were made.\nDocument B shows the police applying the law unevenly, which gives a fuller picture of their role than Document A.",
