    "label": "C2",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "In July 1917 de Valera won East Clare by a large majority, and in October 1917 he was elected president of Sinn Féin. He founded Fianna Fáil in May 1926, and it entered the Dáil in 1927 and won power in 1932 under his leadership. His alternative Document No. 2 was never adopted, and after the Dáil approved the Treaty by 64 votes to 57 he resigned as President on 9 January 1922. In 1938 the Anglo-Irish Agreements returned the Treaty ports to Ireland and settled the annuities dispute. He kept Ireland neutral in the Second World War, and the 1937 constitution he drafted replaced the Free State constitution. He failed to end partition, as Britain would not move on the border, and the Economic War cost the farming economy dearly.",
