    "label": "C3",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Cosgrave headed the government from 1922 and held the state together through the Army Mutiny of March 1924 and the assassination of Kevin O'Higgins in 1927. The Civic Guard, renamed the Garda Síochána in 1923, was set up as an unarmed police force, and the Courts of Justice Act 1924 created a new court system. The Free State joined the League of Nations in 1923 and opened a legation in Washington in 1924. The Land Act of 1923 completed the transfer of land to tenants by compulsory purchase of untenanted land. The Shannon Scheme, approved in 1925 and opened at Ardnacrusha in 1929, and the Electricity Supply Board set up in 1927 gave the state a modern electricity system. In March 1932 he handed over power peacefully after the Fianna Fáil election victory, the first democratic transfer of power in the new state.",
