    "label": "C2",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Giuseppe Mazzini, born in Genoa in 1805, wanted a single unified Italian republic in which the people were sovereign, and his motto was God and the People. In 1831 he founded Young Italy at Marseille, a secret society whose members swore to work for an independent united republic. He organised the failed invasion of Savoy in 1834 and founded Young Europe in the same year to link revolutionary movements across the continent. In 1849 he governed the Roman Republic as one of its triumvirs. He rejected the monarchy of 1861 as a betrayal of his ideal, and in 1870 he was arrested in Sicily while trying to start a republican rising. His achievement was to inspire the nationalist movement, although his republic was never realised and unity came under the Piedmontese monarchy.",
