    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The motor car developed in Germany and France in the 1880s from the internal combustion engine. Nikolaus Otto built the first practical four-stroke engine, which burned gas, in 1876. Gottlieb Daimler and Wilhelm Maybach fitted their small, high-speed petrol engine to a motorcycle in 1885 and to a carriage in 1886. Karl Benz patented his Motorwagen in 1886, and it is regarded as the first practical car designed as a whole. In August 1888 his wife Bertha drove it about 106 km from Mannheim to Pforzheim, which showed that the car could be useful.",
