    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Lenin returned to Russia in April 1917 and issued the April Theses, calling for power to pass to the soviets. He led the Bolsheviks in seizing power in October 1917 and presided over the Council of People's Commissars, the first Soviet government. In the civil war he authorised terror through the Cheka, and War Communism nationalised industry and forced peasants to hand over grain. At the Tenth Party Congress in March 1921 he introduced the New Economic Policy, which allowed small private trade and peasant sales of surplus grain. Lenin died on 21 January 1924, leaving the party without a clear successor.",
