    "label": "B2",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Hitler took Germany out of the League of Nations and the Disarmament Conference in October 1933, and in March 1935 he announced conscription and an air force in breach of Versailles. He reoccupied the Rhineland on 7 March 1936, and Britain and France did not resist militarily. He annexed Austria in the Anschluss of March 1938, and at Munich in September 1938 Britain and France accepted German demands for the Sudetenland. German troops entered Prague in March 1939, and the Nazi-Soviet Pact of August 1939 removed the threat of war on two fronts before the invasion of Poland.",
