    "label": "B4",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "About six million Jews were murdered in the Holocaust, and the killing was carried out across occupied Europe. Mobile Einsatzgruppen followed the German army into the Soviet Union from June 1941 and carried out mass shootings, including the killing of about 33,000 Jews at Babi Yar near Kiev in September 1941. The Wannsee Conference of 20 January 1942, chaired by Reinhard Heydrich, coordinated the deportation and murder of European Jews under the Final Solution. Between 1942 and 1944 most Jews deported from occupied Europe were killed at death camps such as Auschwitz-Birkenau and Treblinka. Allied governments received reports of the murders from 1942 but were slow to act.",
