    "label": "B3",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Lome Conventions were trade and aid agreements between the European Economic Community and the ACP states, beginning with Lome I, which was signed on 28 February 1975. Lome I gave ACP exports largely duty-free access to European markets without requiring reciprocal concessions. STABEX compensated ACP countries when earnings from specified agricultural exports fell, and Lome II added SYSMIN to help mineral exporters. The later Conventions added conditions on human rights and governance, and the Cotonou Agreement replaced them in 2000.",
