    "label": "C3",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Sukarno founded the Indonesian Nationalist Party in 1927 and was imprisoned by the Dutch in 1929. Under the Japanese occupation he encouraged mass mobilisation, which some Dutch and later Indonesian critics saw as collaboration with Japan. On 1 June 1945 he gave the Pancasila speech, setting out five principles for an independent Indonesia. With Hatta he proclaimed Indonesian independence in Jakarta on 17 August 1945 and became the first president of the Republic. Under Guided Democracy from 1959 he ended parliamentary government and promoted Nasakom, the union of nationalism, religion and communism. His real power ended with the coup attempt of 30 September 1965 and the Supersemar order of 11 March 1966, which left General Suharto in control.",
