    "model": "Robert Peel founded the Metropolitan Police in London in 1829 as Home Secretary, creating a professional force that became a model for other cities. His Tamworth Manifesto of 1834 set out a moderate programme of Conservative reform that became the basis of the modern Conservative Party. As Prime Minister he reintroduced income tax in 1842 to pay for cuts in tariffs on imports. In 1846 he repealed the Corn Laws, a victory for free trade, which split the Conservative Party and led to his resignation.",
