    "label": "B2",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Leo XIII was elected pope on 20 February 1878 and reigned until 1903, trying to renew the Church's relations with the modern world. He ended the Kulturkampf by negotiation with Bismarck during the 1880s. In his encyclical Rerum Novarum of 1891 he defended private property and rejected socialism, but he upheld the right of workers to a just wage and to form trade unions. His ralliement policy urged French Catholics to accept the Third Republic, but monarchist Catholics largely refused and the policy failed.",
