    "label": "C4",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Marie Curie was born in Warsaw in 1867 and studied physics at the Sorbonne in Paris from 1891. With her husband Pierre she researched radioactivity, a term she coined, and in 1898 they announced the discovery of polonium and radium. She shared the 1903 Nobel Prize for Physics and won the 1911 Nobel Prize for Chemistry, making her the first person to win Nobel Prizes in two sciences. After Pierre was killed in 1906 she became the first woman professor at the Sorbonne. During the First World War she organised mobile X-ray units for field hospitals, and she founded the Radium Institute in Paris in 1914. Her work made her one of the most important scientists of the period and a pioneer for women in science.",
