    "model": "The first Moscow trial of August 1936 tried Zinoviev and Kamenev, who confessed in open court and were shot within hours of the verdict. The second trial of January 1937 charged Pyatakov and Radek with wrecking in factories and mines, which explained the failures of the Five-Year Plans. The third trial of March 1938 tried Bukharin, Rykov and Yagoda, and eighteen defendants were shot. The NKVD obtained confessions by sleep deprivation, threats and, from 1937, physical torture, and the verdicts were decided in advance.",
