    "label": "B4",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Bing Crosby sang with a jazz band before becoming a radio singer in the early 1930s, when he developed a relaxed crooning style suited to the microphone. He made hundreds of records and starred in films, including the Road series with Bob Hope from 1940, and he won the Academy Award for Best Actor for Going My Way. His recording of White Christmas, released in 1942 for Holiday Inn, became one of the best-selling songs of all time and was hugely popular with troops. He entertained Allied troops through radio broadcasts and USO tours, including a tour of Britain and France in 1944.",
