    "label": "C1",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Hitler took Germany out of the League of Nations and the Geneva Disarmament Conference in October 1933, citing unequal treatment. In March 1935 he announced conscription and an air force in breach of the Treaty of Versailles. He reoccupied the Rhineland on 7 March 1936 without military resistance from Britain or France. He annexed Austria in the Anschluss of 12 March 1938, after forcing Chancellor Schuschnigg to cancel a plebiscite. At Munich in September 1938 Britain and France accepted Hitler's demands for the Sudetenland without consulting Czechoslovakia. German troops entered Prague on 15 March 1939, breaking the Munich promises. The Nazi-Soviet Pact of August 1939 removed the threat of war on two fronts, and Germany invaded Poland on 1 September 1939.",
