    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Soviet Union blockaded road, rail and canal access to West Berlin from June 1948, after the Western zones introduced the Deutsche Mark on 20 June 1948. The Western powers organised an airlift that flew food, fuel and other supplies into the Tempelhof, Gatow and Tegel airfields. The airlift delivered over two million tons before the blockade was lifted on 12 May 1949. Truman refused to withdraw, and the failure of the blockade was followed by the founding of the Federal Republic of Germany on 23 May 1949 and of NATO.",
