    "model": "The Yom Kippur War began on 6 October 1973, and on 16 October OPEC's Gulf members raised the posted oil price by about 70 per cent. Arab oil-producing states announced output cuts and an embargo on oil exports to the USA and the Netherlands because they supported Israel. Oil prices roughly quadrupled in the months that followed, and the high prices remained after the embargo was lifted in March 1974. The shock brought fuel rationing, car-free Sundays and a three-day working week in Britain, and it led to recession, high inflation and rising unemployment.",
