    "model": "Gorbachev became General Secretary in March 1985 and introduced glasnost, greater openness that allowed criticism of officials and freer discussion of the Soviet past. His perestroika programme aimed to restructure the economy by adding limited market mechanisms to central planning. He met Reagan at Geneva in 1985 and Reykjavik in 1986, and the INF Treaty of December 1987 eliminated intermediate-range missiles. He withdrew Soviet forces from Afghanistan by February 1989, and in December 1988 he announced cuts of 500,000 men and the withdrawal of divisions from eastern Europe. Under the Sinatra Doctrine he did not use force in eastern Europe, so communist states could choose their own paths. His reforms weakened the party's control and encouraged the republics to demand independence, and the Soviet Union was dissolved on 26 December 1991.",
