    "model": "In June 1958 de Gaulle told the settlers 'Je vous ai compris' and at Mostaganem he cried 'Vive l'Algérie française', so many settlers believed he would keep Algeria French. On 16 September 1959 he changed course and offered Algerians self-determination, a choice between independence, integration with France or a form of association. In January 1960 he put down the settler revolt known as Barricades Week with the army. In a referendum on 8 January 1961 about 75 per cent of votes cast overall approved self-determination. When generals seized Algiers in the April 1961 putsch, the coup failed after four days because the army and conscripts stayed loyal to him. He then signed the Évian Accords with the FLN on 18 March 1962, and Algeria became independent on 5 July 1962.",
