    "model": "Sukarno founded the Indonesian Nationalist Party (PNI) in 1927, and the Dutch imprisoned him in 1929 before exiling him to remote islands. On 1 June 1945 he set out the Pancasila, five principles on which an independent Indonesia would be based. He and Mohammad Hatta proclaimed Indonesian independence in Jakarta on 17 August 1945, and he became the first president of the Republic. At the Bandung Conference in April 1955 he was the most prominent host of 29 Asian and African countries, which promoted non-alignment and anti-colonialism. On 5 July 1959 he introduced Guided Democracy by decree, ending parliamentary government and ruling with a National Front and the army. He also gave the nation Indonesian as a national language and a unifying ideology, although his rule ended in the 1965 coup attempt and the killings that followed.",
