    "model": "Michael Harrington's The Other America (1962) drew attention to the tens of millions of Americans living in poverty, and Johnson declared a War on Poverty in January 1964. Nixon declared drug abuse public enemy number one in 1971, and crack cocaine spread through poor urban neighbourhoods in the mid-1980s. The Anti-Drug Abuse Act of 1986 set mandatory sentences that treated one gram of crack the same as one hundred grams of powder cocaine. Black Americans were imprisoned at several times the rate of white men, and urban riots in Watts in 1965 and Detroit in 1967 showed the anger of poor black neighbourhoods.",
