    "label": "C3",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "The Moon landing fulfilled Kennedy's pledge of 25 May 1961 to land a man on the Moon before the decade ended. It gave the United States a Cold War victory over the Soviet Union, whose N1 Moon rocket failed in every test. About 600 million people watched the landing live on television, making it one of the most watched events in history. The Apollo programme showed the power of American technology, and the Apollo Guidance Computer was one of the first to use integrated circuits. The landing ended the race to the Moon, although NASA's budget fell after 1969 and public support declined. The achievement became a symbol of American national pride around the world.",
