    "label": "2(a)",
    "marks": 10,
    "model": "Yes, the two documents give largely similar descriptions of the activities of the strike supporters.\nDocument A describes UDA men setting fire to stolen lorries, cars and bicycles on makeshift barricades, so Belfast looked like a city in revolt.\nDocument B describes a Loyalist mob of UWC strike supporters pushing hijacked cars and vans together to form a barricade blocking the road.\nBoth documents show barricades built from stolen or hijacked vehicles.\nBoth documents also show the strikers breaking the law, as Document A describes a container lorry being hijacked and Document B describes a mob blocking the road.",
