    "model": "Yeats co-founded the National Literary Society in Dublin in 1892 and the Irish Literary Theatre in 1899 with Lady Gregory and Edward Martyn. His play The Countess Cathleen was staged in 1899 and was attacked by Catholic critics as heretical. He helped open the Abbey Theatre in December 1904 as one of its directors, alongside Lady Gregory and J.M. Synge. His early poetry, such as The Wanderings of Oisin in 1889, drew on Irish mythology and helped create a national literature.",
