    "label": "C4",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Wilson kept the USA neutral until 1917, and when Germany resumed unrestricted submarine warfare and the Zimmermann Telegram was published, he asked Congress to declare war on 2 April 1917. American troops brought fresh strength to the Allies in 1918. In January 1918 he announced the Fourteen Points, which became the basis for Germany's request for an armistice. Point 14 proposed a League of Nations to guarantee the independence of all states. At the Paris Peace Conference he insisted that the League Covenant be part of the treaty. To win agreement he accepted reparations, Article 231 and Japanese gains in Shandong. However, the Republican Senate led by Henry Cabot Lodge rejected the treaty because Wilson refused to compromise, and his stroke in October 1919 ended his influence.",
