    "model": "Leni Riefenstahl was a film-maker whose documentaries of the Nazi rallies and the 1936 Olympics gave the regime its most influential visual image, after Hitler commissioned her to film the party rallies. She directed Triumph of the Will (1935), which recorded the 1934 Nuremberg Rally and won the German National Film Prize. Her documentary Olympia (1938) presented athletic achievement as a national triumph, using innovative camera techniques. After 1945 she claimed her films were artistic rather than propaganda, and she was classified as a fellow traveller in 1952, but historians judge her films among the most effective propaganda ever made.",
