    "label": "B2",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Churchill became Prime Minister on 10 May 1940 and also acted as Minister of Defence. His speeches, such as 'blood, toil, tears and sweat' and 'their finest hour', sustained British morale after Dunkirk and during the Blitz. He built a close relationship with President Roosevelt, meeting him at Casablanca in January 1943, where unconditional surrender was announced, and attending the Tehran and Yalta conferences. Historians praise his resolve in 1940 but criticise the bombing of Dresden and his attitude to colonial peoples during the Bengal famine of 1943.",
