    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Nuremberg Laws of 15 September 1935 defined Jews by descent, removed their German citizenship and banned marriage between Jews and people of German blood. On Kristallnacht, 9 and 10 November 1938, Nazi supporters and the SA destroyed over 250 synagogues and killed about 90 Jews, and about 30,000 Jewish men were then sent to concentration camps. At the Wannsee Conference on 20 January 1942, chaired by Reinhard Heydrich, the deportation and murder of European Jewry under the Final Solution was coordinated. About six million Jews were murdered in the Holocaust, most of them in death camps such as Auschwitz-Birkenau.",
