    "model": "Bing Crosby was an American singer and actor whose radio shows, records and films made him the most popular entertainer of his age. He developed a relaxed crooning style after becoming a radio singer in the early 1930s, and his music spread the sound of American radio into Europe. His recording of White Christmas, released in 1942 for the film Holiday Inn, became one of the best-selling songs of all time and was hugely popular with troops. He starred with Bob Hope in the Road series from 1940 and won the Academy Award for Best Actor for Going My Way at the 1945 ceremony. During the war he entertained Allied troops through radio broadcasts and USO tours, including a tour of Britain and France in 1944. Historians treat him as a key figure in the development of the modern popular music industry, and he embodied easy-going American popular culture.",
