    "model": "Marshall Aid was the American programme of economic aid to Western Europe, known as the European Recovery Programme, which ran from 1948 to 1952. It provided about 13 billion dollars, mostly as grants rather than loans, to help Western European recovery. Recipients had to draw up recovery plans, and the Organisation for European Economic Co-operation, set up in April 1948, coordinated the aid. Britain, France and West Germany received the largest sums, and the aid encouraged states to remove trade barriers and cooperate on trade and payments.",
