    "model": "Lennon was born in Liverpool in 1940 and formed the Quarrymen in 1957, which later became The Beatles with Paul McCartney, George Harrison and Ringo Starr. The Beatles' long residencies in Hamburg and their first UK number one, From Me to You in 1963, built their popularity in Britain. His 1966 remark that the Beatles were more popular than Jesus provoked protests and record burnings in parts of the USA. After the Beatles he recorded Imagine in 1971, and he was shot dead in New York on 8 December 1980, a death widely mourned across Europe and America.",
