    "marks": 40,
    "model": "On 13 May 1958 settlers and army officers seized government buildings in Algiers, and the National Assembly invested de Gaulle as prime minister on 1 June 1958. On 16 September 1959 he announced that Algerians would be offered self-determination, a choice between independence, integration and association. In a referendum on 8 January 1961, about 75 per cent of voters approved self-determination. The generals' putsch of April 1961 failed after four days because conscripts and the army stayed loyal to him. The OAS responded with bombings and assassinations in Algeria and France, and its ambush of de Gaulle's car at Petit-Clamart in August 1962 failed. The Évian Accords of 18 March 1962 ended the war, and Algeria became independent on 5 July 1962.",
