    "marks": 10,
    "model": "Yes, both visitors show concern about developments in Soviet Russia.\nDocument A: the Coles were 'highly agitated' and Mrs Cole's hands 'trembled nervously' when Maisky scolded them about the trials.\nDocument A: even after Maisky's explanation the Coles were still troubled by the trials and executions.\nDocument B: Dalton said the purges had 'disturbed us a great deal' and feared the executions had seriously weakened the Red Army.",
