    "label": "3(a)",
    "marks": 10,
    "model": "Primary source: it was written at the time, showing how a loyal Stalin supporter explained events as they unfolded.\nCurrent events: it deals with the Kirov killing, which Maisky calls 'striking proof' of the terrorist threat.\nPrivate views: a private diary may show honest views that can be compared with his public statements.\nPersonality: it reveals the writer's character, as he gave the Coles 'a serious ticking off'.\nLimitation, one perspective: it gives only the view of a Soviet diplomat.\nLimitation, honesty: it may not be fully truthful, as Maisky would know that appearing disloyal was dangerous.\nLimitation, distance: his London post kept him away from the centre of power in Moscow.",
