    "marks": 10,
    "model": "Yes, Maisky was a skilful propagandist, as shown in both documents.\nDocument A: he blames a 'large terrorist conspiracy' on the German Nazis, which creates a sense of menace.\nDocument A: he uses the Kirov killing as 'striking proof' that the threat was real.\nDocument A: he forestalls criticism by calling the shootings 'hard and unpleasant' and comparing 80-100 deaths with risking millions of lives on the battlefield.\nDocument B: he tries to persuade Dalton that the generals were pro-German and planning a military dictatorship, so the trials seemed reasonable.\nAgainst: the Coles remained 'still troubled' and Dalton found the account 'almost incredible', so his persuasion was not complete.",
