    "label": "4",
    "marks": 20,
    "model": "The show trials and the Terror that followed destroyed the party's old guard, because Stalin's rivals were dead or in exile, and the new officials who replaced them owed their positions to him. The economy lost many managers, engineers and planners, and fear of being accused of wrecking made officials cautious and encouraged them to falsify results or avoid decisions. The army and the security services were also purged, and the loss of experienced officers is widely linked to the poor Soviet performance against Finland in 1939 and 1940 and the German advance in 1941. Society was affected by fear and denunciations, and the families of those arrested were stigmatised as relatives of enemies of the people.",
