    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Douglas Hyde gave the lecture The Necessity for De-Anglicising Ireland in Dublin on 25 November 1892, arguing that the Irish should revive their own language and customs. He co-founded the Gaelic League in July 1893 and led it until 1915, building mass interest in the Irish language through classes and festivals. He also published collections of Gaelic songs and folktales, including Love Songs of Connacht in 1893. W.B. Yeats helped found the National Literary Society in 1892 and the Irish Literary Theatre in 1899. His early poetry, such as The Wanderings of Oisin, drew on Irish mythology. He helped open the Abbey Theatre in December 1904 as one of its three directors.",
