    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Bernadette Devlin was a student leader in People's Democracy, which organised the Belfast to Derry march of January 1969. She was elected MP for Mid Ulster in April 1969, aged twenty-one, as a candidate of the unity and civil rights movement. She was convicted of incitement to riot after the Battle of the Bogside in August 1969, and she served a prison sentence in 1970. On 31 January 1972, the day after Bloody Sunday, she struck the Home Secretary Reginald Maudling in the House of Commons.",
