    "label": "B4",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Downing Street Declaration was issued on 15 December 1993 by John Major and Albert Reynolds. It accepted that the Irish people as a whole had the right to self-determination. The British government stated that it had no selfish strategic or economic interest in Northern Ireland. It said a united Ireland would require the consent of a majority in Northern Ireland. It invited republicans to renounce violence and join talks, and it committed the Irish government to a forum for peace and reconciliation.",
