    "label": "C4",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "John Hume chaired the University for Derry campaign in 1964 and 1965, uniting nationalists and some unionists behind a single campaign for the city. In 1968 he became vice-chairman of the Derry Citizens' Action Committee, formed after the civil rights march of 5 October 1968. He was a founder of the SDLP in 1970 and became Minister of Commerce in the power-sharing executive in January 1974. At Sunningdale he was a leading SDLP negotiator, and he defended the executive during the strike of May 1974. He became leader of the SDLP in 1979 and supported the Anglo-Irish Agreement as a role for nationalists in government. From 1988 he held talks with Gerry Adams, arguing that the IRA campaign must end if nationalists were to achieve their goals by dialogue. His dialogue with Sinn Féin and his work with Dublin influenced the Downing Street Declaration of 1993.",
