    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Breandán Ó hEithir was a writer, journalist and broadcaster who was born on Inis Mór, one of the Aran Islands, in 1930. He worked for RTÉ, presenting current affairs and cultural and sporting programmes in both Irish and English, and he wrote a regular newspaper column. His novel Lig Sinn i gCathú, published in 1976, was widely read in Irish, and he translated it himself as Lead Us into Temptation. His Over the Bar, a personal history of the GAA, and his witty account of political life, The Begrudger's Guide to Irish Politics, reached a wide English-speaking audience.",
