    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Metternich, Austrian foreign minister from 1809 and state chancellor from 1821, sought to preserve the 1815 settlement and the multinational Habsburg Empire. He used the Congress System, including the Troppau Protocol and the Laibach congress of 1821, to justify intervention against revolutions, and Austrian troops crushed risings in Italy in 1821 and 1831. Inside Austria, police, informers and strict censorship silenced critics, and the Carlsbad Decrees of 1819 banned the Burschenschaften and imposed censorship on the press. His system collapsed in March 1848 when he was forced to resign after the Vienna rising and fled into exile in England.",
