    "model": "Haussmann improved the water supply, as Belgrand's aqueducts brought clean water from the Dhuis and Vanne valleys into the city. Belgrand's underground sewers carried waste away from the centre, which reduced disease and improved sanitation. Wide straight boulevards improved traffic flow and let troops move quickly through the city. Parks such as the Bois de Boulogne, redesigned in the 1850s, and the Buttes-Chaumont, opened in 1867, gave residents green space. The new Paris Opera and the iron-and-glass Les Halles added impressive public buildings. The annexation of the suburbs in 1860 allowed him to plan the whole urban area.",
