    "model": "David Ben-Gurion led the Jewish Agency's executive from 1935 and accepted the 1947 UN partition plan as a first step towards a Jewish state, even though the Arab states rejected it. He proclaimed the State of Israel in Tel Aviv on 14 May 1948 and became its first prime minister, and five Arab armies invaded the next day. He oversaw the creation of the Israel Defence Forces in May 1948, drawing on the Haganah, and ordered the shelling of the Irgun ship Altalena in June 1948 so that Israel would have only one army. He led Israel through the 1948-49 war, which ended with the 1949 armistice agreements leaving Israel with more territory than the UN plan had allotted. In October 1956 he attended the secret talks at Sèvres with Britain and France that planned the Israeli attack on Sinai during the Suez Crisis. He kept the defence ministry as well as the premiership, so he directed Israel's response to Arab hostility himself.",
