    "model": "Both documents question the value of marching on London, but Document A does so more strongly.\nDocument A says such marches 'can do no good' and are 'altogether undesirable'.\nIt adds that marches have no 'constitutional influence' and that ministers will not 'consent' to receive marchers.\nDocument B says 'these weary marches certainly are useless' and that their real purpose may be propagandist.\nHowever, it recognises the 'desperate conditions' in Jarrow and says parliaments can be 'forgetful, unimaginative, and lazy'.",
