    "label": "3(b)",
    "marks": 10,
    "model": "Document B shows the value of an editorial as a primary source because it was written while the march was in progress.\nAn editorial is an opinion piece that gives the editor's view rather than a full account.\nThe editor had no first-hand experience of the march and relied on other reports.\nIt shows how the march was viewed at the time, agreeing the marches 'certainly are useless' but finding the government's view 'too narrow'.\nIt shows public sympathy, describing the march as 'a plea for work'.\nIts limitation is that it lacks detailed factual information, so historians also need news reports.",
