    "label": "C3",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "The 31st International Eucharistic Congress was held in Dublin from 22 to 26 June 1932 to mark the 1,500th anniversary of St Patrick's arrival in Ireland. Cardinal Lorenzo Lauri, the Pope's legate, arrived at Dún Laoghaire on 21 June and was escorted through crowds of schoolchildren to Dublin. On 25 June about 100,000 children attended a Mass in the Phoenix Park. The closing Mass on 26 June was attended by a crowd put at around a million, and a message from Pope Pius XI was broadcast live by radio to the crowd. The Congress passed off without major disorder and gave the Free State international publicity as a Catholic country. It showed the alliance between the hierarchy and the government that shaped the 1937 constitution, and de Valera used it to present his government as both Catholic and independent of the Crown.",
