    "label": "B2",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "The Molly Maguires were a secret society of Irish miners in the Pennsylvania anthracite coalfields, drawing on the tradition of the Ribbonmen. Franklin B. Gowen, owner of the Reading Railroad, hired the Pinkerton detective James McParland, who infiltrated the society under the name James McKenna. After the failed Long Strike of 1875 the miners' union was broken, and the trials of 1876 to 1878 depended heavily on informers. Ten men were hanged on 21 June 1877, the Day of the Rope, and twenty were hanged in all between 1877 and 1879.",
