    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Terence O'Neill succeeded Brookeborough as Prime Minister in March 1963, after serving as Minister of Finance from 1956. He promoted economic planning, including the Wilson Plan of 1965, which led to the new city of Craigavon. In January 1965 he received the Taoiseach, Seán Lemass, at Stormont, the first meeting between the heads of the two governments since partition. He pursued bridge-building with Catholics and the Republic, and he made symbolic visits to Catholic schools and hospitals. His authority collapsed under civil rights pressure, and he announced a five-point reform package in November 1968 before resigning on 28 April 1969.",
