    "label": "C2",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Nikolaus Otto built the first practical four-stroke engine in 1876, and it became the basis of the petrol engine. Karl Benz's Motorwagen, patented in 1886, is regarded as the first practical car designed as a whole. In August 1888 Bertha Benz drove it about 106 km from Mannheim to Pforzheim, which proved its usefulness. France led early car production, as Panhard et Levassor and Peugeot began building cars in 1890-91 and Louis Renault built his first car in 1898. In 1908 Henry Ford launched the Model T, and in 1913 the moving assembly line at Highland Park cut the time to build a chassis from over twelve hours to about ninety minutes. By 1920 the USA had millions of cars and produced most of the world's cars.",
