    "label": "B2",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Marshall Aid was announced by George Marshall in a speech at Harvard on 5 June 1947 as the European Recovery Programme, the US aid programme for Western Europe. About 13 billion dollars was provided, mostly as grants, and Britain, France and West Germany received the largest sums. The OEEC, set up in April 1948, coordinated the allocation of the aid among the sixteen recipient states. The aid encouraged Western European states to remove trade barriers and reduce inflation, and it supported Christian Democratic and social democratic parties against the communists.",
