    "model": "Nasser nationalised the Suez Canal Company on 26 July 1956 and promised that its revenue would fund the Aswan High Dam. Britain and France planned an attack with Israel, and Israeli forces entered Sinai on 29 October 1956, followed by Anglo-French bombing of Egyptian airfields. The United Nations created UNEF in November 1956 to supervise the withdrawal and the Sinai frontier. American pressure forced the ceasefire: Britain faced a run on the pound, and the IMF refused support until Britain agreed to withdraw, so the ceasefire took effect on 6-7 November.",
