    "marks": 30,
    "model": "When settlers and army officers seized Algiers in May 1958, de Gaulle returned to power and told the settlers 'Je vous ai compris'. On 16 September 1959 he announced that Algerians would be offered self-determination, a choice between independence, integration and association. In April 1961 a group of generals seized Algiers in an attempt to stop independence, but the putsch failed after four days. The Évian Accords of March 1962 set out a ceasefire and the terms of Algerian independence.",
