    "label": "C1",
    "marks": 40,
    "model": "Fidel Castro's revolution took power in Cuba on 1 January 1959, and in 1960 his government nationalised US-owned sugar, oil and other property. Eisenhower cut the Cuban sugar quota in July 1960, imposed a trade embargo and broke off diplomatic relations in January 1961, so Cuba turned to the Soviet Union. CIA-trained Cuban exiles landed at the Bay of Pigs on 17 April 1961 and were defeated within three days, a humiliation for Kennedy. Soviet medium-range missiles were shipped to Cuba from September 1962, and US U-2 photographs of 14 October revealed the launch sites. Kennedy imposed a naval quarantine on 22 October, and on 28 October Khrushchev agreed to remove the missiles in return for a US pledge not to invade Cuba. Kennedy also secretly agreed to withdraw US Jupiter missiles from Turkey, a deal kept private for years.",
