    "label": "3(b)",
    "marks": 10,
    "model": "Document B was written in 1887, only three years after the GAA was founded, so it shows the association growing in north Cork.\nIt shows the pride, discipline and power of the GAA beyond sport, with clubs marching in order before the Archbishop's carriage.\nIt quotes Archbishop Croke, an important early patron of the GAA, who declared that the Association had progressed amazingly.\nIt gives insight into social problems of the time, such as bad blood, drink and neglect of Sunday worship.\nIt suggests the power of the Catholic Church in late nineteenth-century Ireland, since the Archbishop's approval and Sunday Mass mattered to the GAA.",
