    "marks": 20,
    "model": "The GAA spread quickly across the south and west after its founding at Thurles in 1884, and within a few years hundreds of clubs had affiliated. Davin drew up the first rules for hurling and Gaelic football in 1885, and the first All-Ireland championships were held in 1887. The GAA banned members from playing foreign games such as cricket, rugby and soccer, and barred members of the RIC and British forces. The IRB infiltrated the association, and the American tour of 1888 lost money, so by 1891 membership had collapsed.",
