    "label": "B1",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Conn and Patricia McCluskey founded the Campaign for Social Justice in Dungannon in January 1964. Conn McCluskey was a local doctor, and the campaign gathered evidence of discrimination in housing and jobs, especially by councils in Tyrone and Fermanagh. The campaign published its findings and lobbied British MPs at Westminster. Historians credit it with turning discrimination into a public issue before the Civil Rights Association was formed in 1967. Their evidence provided models for the civil rights movement that followed.",
