    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Ireland was admitted to the United Nations on 14 December 1955, after the Soviet Union had vetoed its earlier application in 1946. Frederick Boland was elected President of the General Assembly in 1960, and Ireland served on the Security Council in 1962. Irish troops served in the Congo from 1960, where an Irish patrol was ambushed at Niemba in November 1960 and nine soldiers were killed. From 1978 an Irish battalion served with UNIFIL in Lebanon, after Israel's invasion of southern Lebanon.",
