    "label": "B2",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Germany left the League of Nations and the Geneva Disarmament Conference on 14 October 1933, citing unequal treatment. Hitler announced conscription and an air force on 16 March 1935, in breach of the Treaty of Versailles, and German troops reoccupied the Rhineland on 7 March 1936 without resistance from Britain or France. The Anschluss of 12 March 1938 annexed Austria after German pressure forced Chancellor Schuschnigg to cancel his plebiscite and resign. The Munich Agreement of September 1938 gave Germany the Sudetenland, and German troops entered Prague on 15 March 1939 before Germany invaded Poland on 1 September 1939.",
