    "label": "B3",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "German forces invaded France and the Low Countries on 10 May 1940, and armoured divisions broke through the Ardennes to reach the Channel coast at Abbeville by 20 May, cutting off the British and French armies in the north. France had as many tanks as Germany but spread them among infantry units instead of concentrating them in armoured divisions, and its generals had believed the Ardennes difficult terrain for tanks. Between 26 May and 4 June 1940 the British Expeditionary Force and many French troops were evacuated from Dunkirk. Paris was occupied on 14 June, and on 22 June an armistice signed at Compiègne divided France into an occupied zone and an unoccupied zone.",
