    "model": "Marshall Aid was the American programme of economic aid to Western Europe, announced by Secretary of State George Marshall in June 1947. It provided about 13 billion dollars, mostly as grants, through the European Recovery Programme from 1948 to 1952. Sixteen European states shared the aid, which was coordinated by the Organisation for European Economic Co-operation set up in 1948. The USA hoped to rebuild Western economies and weaken the appeal of communism, but Stalin forbade eastern states to take part, dividing Europe into two economic systems.",
