    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Attlee's Labour government, which won the July 1945 election, was committed to Indian self-rule and argued that Britain could not hold India against the will of its people. The Cabinet Mission of March to June 1946 proposed a loose federal India, but it failed to win agreement between Congress and the League. Lord Mountbatten arrived as Viceroy on 22 March 1947 and pressed for a quick transfer of power. His plan of 3 June 1947 accepted partition and brought the date of independence forward to 15 August 1947.",
