    "model": "Marilyn Monroe, born Norma Jeane Mortenson, became one of the decade's most popular box office stars with Gentlemen Prefer Blondes in 1953. Her glamorous screen image, in films such as The Seven Year Itch (1955), was widely copied in advertising and tied her to the consumer culture of the 1950s. She founded Marilyn Monroe Productions in 1955 to take more control of her career, and she won acclaim for her comic role in Some Like It Hot (1959). She died at her Los Angeles home on 4 August 1962 from an overdose of barbiturates, and the death was ruled a probable suicide.",
