    "label": "B3",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Born Cassius Clay in Louisville in 1942, Ali won Olympic gold at Rome in 1960 and beat Sonny Liston in 1964 to take the world heavyweight title, then took the name Muhammad Ali. He refused induction into the army on 28 April 1967 as a Muslim minister and conscientious objector, and boxing authorities stripped him of his title. The Supreme Court overturned his draft evasion conviction in June 1971 by 8 votes to 0. He regained the heavyweight title by beating George Foreman in Kinshasa in 1974, and he became an international symbol of black pride and resistance to the Vietnam War.",
