    "model": "Cesar Chavez led the Chicano movement's campaign for farm workers, and the Delano grape strike and boycott from 1965 won national support for the United Farm Workers. The American Indian Movement was founded in Minneapolis in 1968, and its activists occupied Alcatraz Island from 1969 to 1971 and Wounded Knee in 1973. The Stonewall riots of June 1969 led to the founding of the Gay Liberation Front, and marches commemorating Stonewall began in 1970. The Bilingual Education Act of 1968 gave a legal basis to minority languages in schools, and the television series Roots (1977) drew about 100 million viewers.",
