    "model": "President Kennedy committed the United States in May 1961 to landing a man on the Moon before the decade ended, and NASA chose lunar orbit rendezvous in 1962 as the method. The Gemini missions of 1965 and 1966 tested the rendezvous and docking that this method needed. Apollo 11 was launched from Florida on 16 July 1969, and its lunar module Eagle landed on the Moon on 20 July. Neil Armstrong and Edwin Aldrin spent about two and a half hours on the surface, collecting about 21 kilograms of rock and soil. The mission was a Cold War victory over the Soviet Union, whose Moon rocket failed in every test. Its live broadcast reached an audience of about 600 million people, making American technology an image for the whole world.",
